{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017pgcuRwqUxzMLdC6WZCGbY","type":"tool_result","content":" 05:41:07 up 13 days, 17:45,  1 user,  load average: 1.14, 3.17, 6.06\nEXIT 0","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b8bb938-d2d7-4b06-928c-41c6584adc85","uuid":"bf767dc8-6cdf-479f-9b03-012e1f093d5f","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:41:57.272Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":" 05:41:07 up 13 days, 17:45,  1 user,  load average: 1.14, 3.17, 6.06\nEXIT 0","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":true,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/09_assembly/check.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":330,"lines":["+#!/usr/bin/env python3","+\"\"\"Item 09 of loop0012: the pathwidth assembly of `DegreeBound/Pathwidth.lean`, checked","+in the form the file proves it, before it is stated.","+","+The hypotheses (H1), (H3) are named `Prop`s and cannot be checked; what is checked is every","+*deterministic* statement the assembly rests on, on every graph on 1..8 vertices","+(`nauty-geng`, 13,598 graphs; pathwidth by the subset DP of","+`learning.edwards_mcdermid.pathwidth_induced`), and the numerical pin of the item on 500","+random graphs at `n ≤ 12`:","+","+  PB   pathwidth ⊥ = 0                                        (`pathwidth_bot`)","+  IX   pw(G) ≤ pw(G − X) + |X| for every X ⊆ V                 (`pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card`)","+  IXc  pw(G[Xᶜ]) ≤ pw(G − X)                                   (`pathwidth_induce_compl_le_isolateSet`)","+  I1   pw(G) ≤ pw(G − v) + 1                                   (`pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolate_add_one`)","+  CR   pw(G[C₀]) ≤ pw(G|C₀) for every component C₀             (`pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le_restrict`)","+  CM   C connected, v ∈ C ⇒ C ⊆ C₀(v) and pw(G[C]) ≤ pw(G[C₀])  (`subset_compFinset_of_connected`, `pathwidth_induce_mono`)","+  CC   G[C₀] is connected for every component                   (`connected_induce_compFinset`)","+  ID   v ∈ C₀ ⇒ deg_{G[C₀]}(v) = deg_G(v)                       (`degree_induce_compFinset`)","+  EZ   every degree of C zero ⇒ G[C] = ⊥, pw = 0                 (`induce_eq_bot_of_forall_degree_eq_zero`)","+  FC   pw(G) = max over connected C of pw(G[C]) (0 if none)      (`pathwidth_le_rat_of_forall_connected`)","+  BC   for reduced basic B ≠ ⊥, each non-trivial component C₀: cubic ⇒ measure","+       τ_need = pw(B[C₀]) − (|C₀|/6 − 1/6); second kind ⇒ some u ∈ C₀ has r(B|C₀ − u) = ∅","+       and pw(B[C₀]) ≤ pw(B|C₀ − u) + 1 (measure ρ_need = pw(B|C₀ − u), the (H3) gap at ⊥);","+       and compPotential(C₀) ≤ f⁻(B)                            (`pathwidth_component_le`)","+  A1   reduced G ≠ ⊥, X from Algorithm X (item 02), B = r(G − X): pw(G) ≤ pw(G − X) + |X|,","+       |X| + f⁻(B) ≤ f⁻(G); measure pw(G − X) − pw(B) (the (H3) gap) and pw(G) − f⁻(G)","+       (what τ + 2ρ + 1 must reach)                             (`pathwidth_le_potentialMinus_of_hypotheses`)","+  A2   every G, B = r(G): pw(G) − f(B) and pw(G) − f(G) measured, f(B) ≤ f(G)","+                                                                 (`pathwidth_le_degreeSum_of_hypotheses`, `_histogram_`)","+  PIN  500 random graphs, 1 ≤ n ≤ 12: pw(G) ≤ Σ_{r(G)} g + B(n), B = 3 (n ≤ 9), 10/3 (n = 10),","+       4 (n ≤ 20), item 02 §2.5 and item 01 §1.3's measured budgets (a pipeline check,","+       not a check of the theorem, whose budgets are abstract)","+","+Usage: nice -n 19 python3 check.py --max-n 8 --workers 8","+\"\"\"","+from __future__ import annotations","+","+import argparse","+import collections","+import json","+import os","+import random","+import subprocess","+import sys","+import time","+from fractions import Fraction","+from multiprocessing import Pool","+","+HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))","+sys.path.insert(0, os.path.abspath(os.path.join(HERE, \"..\", \"..\", \"..\", \"..\")))","+","+from learning.edwards_mcdermid import (  # noqa: E402","+    algorithm_x, bits, components, f_potential, fminus, g, g_prime, is_basic, is_reduced,","+    isolate, isolate_set, main_term, min_degree, parse_g6, pathwidth_induced, reduce, restrict,","+    support,","+)","+","+","+def full(n: int) -> int:","+    return (1 << n) - 1","+","+","+def connected_mask(adj: list[int], C: int) -> bool:","+    if C == 0:","+        return False","+    v = (C & -C).bit_length() - 1","+    seen = 1 << v","+    frontier = seen","+    while frontier:","+        nxt = 0","+        for u in bits(frontier):","+            nxt |= adj[u] & C","+        nxt &= ~seen","+        seen |= nxt","+        frontier = nxt","+    return seen == C","+","+","+def comp_potential(adj: list[int], C: int) -> Fraction:","+    return sum((g(adj[v].bit_count()) for v in bits(C)), Fraction(0)) - g_prime(min_degree(adj, C))","+","+","+def check_graph(adj: list[int], rng: random.Random, exhaustive_X: bool) -> tuple[dict, list[str], dict]:","+    \"\"\"One graph: the counters, the violations, the maxima measured.\"\"\"","+    n = len(adj)","+    cnt: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()","+    viol: list[str] = []","+    mx: dict[str, Fraction] = {}","+","+    def bump(key, val):","+        if key not in mx or val > mx[key]:","+            mx[key] = val","+","+    V = full(n)","+    pw = {}","+","+    def pw_of(adj_, S):","+        return pathwidth_induced(adj_, S)","+","+    pwG = pw_of(adj, V)","+    cnt[\"graphs\"] += 1","+    # PB","+    cnt[\"PB\"] += 1","+    if pw_of([0] * n, V) != 0:","+        viol.append(f\"PB n={n}\")","+    # IX, IXc: every X (exhaustive to 8), else 2n random X","+    Xs = range(V + 1) if exhaustive_X else [rng.randrange(V + 1) for _ in range(2 * n)]","+    for X in Xs:","+        GX = isolate_set(adj, X)","+        pwGX = pw_of(GX, V)","+        cnt[\"IX\"] += 1","+        if pwG > pwGX + X.bit_count():","+            viol.append(f\"IX {adj} X={X}\")","+        cnt[\"IXc\"] += 1","+        if pw_of(adj, V & ~X) > pwGX:","+            viol.append(f\"IXc {adj} X={X}\")","+    # I1","+    for v in range(n):","+        cnt[\"I1\"] += 1","+        if pwG > pw_of(isolate(adj, v), V) + 1:","+            viol.append(f\"I1 {adj} v={v}\")","+    # components","+    comps = components(adj, support_only=False)","+    comp_pw = {}","+    for C0 in comps:","+        cnt[\"CC\"] += 1","+        if not connected_mask(adj, C0):","+            viol.append(f\"CC {adj} C0={C0}\")","+        p = pw_of(adj, C0)","+        comp_pw[C0] = p","+        cnt[\"CR\"] += 1","+        if p > pw_of(restrict(adj, C0), V):","+            viol.append(f\"CR {adj} C0={C0}\")","+        for v in bits(C0):","+            cnt[\"ID\"] += 1","+            if (adj[v] & C0).bit_count() != adj[v].bit_count():","+                viol.append(f\"ID {adj} v={v}\")","+    # CM, EZ, FC over every connected subset (exhaustive to 8; sampled above)","+    subsets = range(1, V + 1) if exhaustive_X else [rng.randrange(1, V + 1) for _ in range(4 * n)]","+    best = 0","+    for C in subsets:","+        if not connected_mask(adj, C):","+            continue","+        p = pw_of(adj, C)","+        best = max(best, p)","+        v = (C & -C).bit_length() - 1","+        C0 = next(c for c in comps if (c >> v) & 1)","+        cnt[\"CM\"] += 1","+        if C & ~C0 or p > comp_pw[C0]:","+            viol.append(f\"CM {adj} C={C}\")","+        if all(adj[u] == 0 for u in bits(C)):","+            cnt[\"EZ\"] += 1","+            if p != 0 or C.bit_count() != 1:","+                viol.append(f\"EZ {adj} C={C}\")","+    if exhaustive_X:","+        cnt[\"FC\"] += 1","+        if pwG != best:","+            viol.append(f\"FC {adj} pw={pwG} max={best}\")","+    # BC: reduced basic non-empty","+    if is_reduced(adj) and support(adj) and is_basic(adj):","+        cnt[\"BC_graphs\"] += 1","+        fm = fminus(adj)","+        for C0 in components(adj):","+            cp = comp_potential(adj, C0)","+            cnt[\"BC_components\"] += 1","+            if cp > fm:","+                viol.append(f\"BC_cp_le_fminus {adj} C0={C0}\")","+            p = comp_pw[C0]","+            sub = restrict(adj, C0)","+            if all(adj[v].bit_count() == 3 for v in bits(C0)):","+                cnt[\"BC_cubic\"] += 1","+                if cp != Fraction(C0.bit_count(), 6) - Fraction(1, 6):","+                    viol.append(f\"BC_cubic_cp {adj} C0={C0}\")","+                bump(\"tau_need_cubic\", Fraction(p) - (Fraction(C0.bit_count(), 6) - Fraction(1, 6)))","+            else:","+                us = [u for u in bits(C0) if not any(reduce(isolate(sub, u))[0])]","+                cnt[\"BC_second\"] += 1","+                if not us:","+                    viol.append(f\"BC_second_no_u {adj} C0={C0}\")","+                    continue","+                rho = [pw_of(isolate(sub, u), V) for u in us]","+                if any(p > r + 1 for r in rho):","+                    viol.append(f\"BC_second_pw {adj} C0={C0}\")","+                bump(\"rho_need_second_min_u\", Fraction(min(rho)))","+                bump(\"rho_need_second_max_u\", Fraction(max(rho)))","+                bump(\"pw_minus_cp_second\", Fraction(p) - cp)","+    # A1","+    if is_reduced(adj) and support(adj):","+        cnt[\"A1\"] += 1","+        X, _ = algorithm_x(adj, rng)","+        GX = isolate_set(adj, X)","+        B, _ = reduce(GX)","+        if not (is_reduced(B) and any(B) and is_basic(B)):","+            viol.append(f\"A1_B {adj} X={X}\")","+        pwGX = pw_of(GX, V)","+        pwB = pw_of(B, V)","+        if pwG > pwGX + X.bit_count():","+            viol.append(f\"A1_IX {adj} X={X}\")","+        if X.bit_count() + fminus(B) > fminus(adj):","+            viol.append(f\"A1_T1 {adj} X={X}\")","+        bump(\"rho_need_A1\", Fraction(pwGX - pwB))","+        bump(\"A1_pw_minus_fminus\", Fraction(pwG) - fminus(adj))","+        bump(\"A1_pwB_minus_fminusB\", Fraction(pwB) - fminus(B))","+    # A2","+    cnt[\"A2\"] += 1","+    B, _ = reduce(adj)","+    if f_potential(B) > f_potential(adj):","+        viol.append(f\"A2_f_le {adj}\")","+    bump(\"rho_need_A2\", Fraction(pwG - pw_of(B, V)))","+    bump(\"A2_pw_minus_fB\", Fraction(pwG) - f_potential(B))","+    bump(\"A2_pw_minus_fG\", Fraction(pwG) - f_potential(adj))","+    return dict(cnt), viol, {k: str(v) for k, v in mx.items()}","+","+","+def one(job):","+    i, line, exhaustive = job","+    n, adj = parse_g6(line)","+    rng = random.Random(1109 * 100003 + i)","+    return check_graph(adj, rng, exhaustive)","+","+","+def geng(n: int) -> list[str]:","+    return subprocess.run([\"nauty-geng\", \"-q\", str(n)], capture_output=True, text=True,","+                          check=True).stdout.splitlines()","+","+","+def budget(n: int) -> Fraction:","+    if n <= 9:","+        return Fraction(3)","+    if n == 10:","+        return Fraction(10, 3)","+    return Fraction(4)","+","+","+def pin_job(i):","+    rng = random.Random(1109_000 + i)","+    n = rng.randint(1, 12)","+    p = rng.choice([0.2, 0.35, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9])","+    adj = [0] * n","+    for u in range(n):","+        for v in range(u + 1, n):","+            if rng.random() < p:","+                adj[u] |= 1 << v","+                adj[v] |= 1 << u","+    pw = pathwidth_induced(adj, full(n))","+    mt = main_term(adj)","+    ok = Fraction(pw) <= mt + budget(n)","+    cnt, viol, mx = check_graph(adj, rng, exhaustive_X=False)","+    return {\"n\": n, \"pw\": pw, \"main\": str(mt), \"deficit\": str(Fraction(pw) - mt), \"ok\": ok,","+            \"cnt\": cnt, \"viol\": viol, \"mx\": mx}","+","+","+def merge_mx(acc: dict, mx: dict) -> None:","+    for k, v in mx.items():","+        fv = Fraction(v)","+        if k not in acc or fv > acc[k]:","+            acc[k] = fv","+","+","+def main() -> None:","+    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()","+    ap.add_argument(\"--max-n\", type=int, default=8)","+    ap.add_argument(\"--workers\", type=int, default=8)","+    ap.add_argument(\"--pin\", type=int, default=500)","+    a = ap.parse_args()","+    log = open(f\"{HERE}/check.log\", \"w\")","+","+    def say(s: str = \"\") -> None:","+        print(s, flush=True)","+        log.write(s + \"\\n\")","+        log.flush()","+","+    say(f\"# item 09 brute-force check, {time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S UTC', time.gmtime())}, \"","+        f\"every graph on 1..{a.max_n} vertices (nauty-geng), {a.workers} workers; \"","+        f\"{a.pin} random graphs at n ≤ 12 for the pin\")","+    total: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()","+    per_n: dict[int, dict] = {}","+    mx: dict[str, Fraction] = {}","+    mx_per_n: dict[int, dict] = {}","+    violations: list[str] = []","+    t0 = time.time()","+    with Pool(a.workers) as pool:","+        for n in range(1, a.max_n + 1):","+            lines = geng(n)","+            cnt: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()","+            mxn: dict[str, Fraction] = {}","+            for res in pool.imap_unordered(one, [(i, l, True) for i, l in enumerate(lines)],","+                                           chunksize=64):","+                c, v, m = res","+                cnt.update(c)","+                violations += v","+                merge_mx(mxn, m)","+            per_n[n] = dict(cnt)","+            mx_per_n[n] = {k: str(v) for k, v in mxn.items()}","+            total.update(cnt)","+            merge_mx(mx, {k: str(v) for k, v in mxn.items()})","+            say(f\"n={n}: {len(lines)} graphs; IX {cnt['IX']}, CM {cnt['CM']}, FC {cnt['FC']}, \"","+                f\"BC components {cnt['BC_components']} (cubic {cnt['BC_cubic']}, second kind \"","+                f\"{cnt['BC_second']}), A1 {cnt['A1']}; maxima {mx_per_n[n]}; \"","+                f\"violations so far {len(violations)}; {time.time() - t0:.0f} s\")","+        pin_rows = list(pool.imap_unordered(pin_job, range(a.pin), chunksize=16))","+    pin_ok = sum(1 for r in pin_rows if r[\"ok\"])","+    pin_cnt: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()","+    pin_mx: dict[str, Fraction] = {}","+    for r in pin_rows:","+        pin_cnt.update(r[\"cnt\"])","+        violations += r[\"viol\"]","+        merge_mx(pin_mx, r[\"mx\"])","+    worst = max(pin_rows, key=lambda r: Fraction(r[\"deficit\"]))","+    say(f\"pin: {pin_ok}/{len(pin_rows)} random graphs (n ≤ 12) have pw ≤ Σ_r(G) g + B(n); \"","+        f\"largest deficit {worst['deficit']} at n={worst['n']} (pw {worst['pw']}, main {worst['main']}); \"","+        f\"the deterministic checks on the same graphs: {dict(pin_cnt)}; maxima {{{', '.join(f'{k}: {v}' for k, v in pin_mx.items())}}}; \"","+        f\"violations so far {len(violations)}\")","+    say(f\"TOTAL: {dict(total)}\")","+    say(f\"MAXIMA to n={a.max_n}: {{{', '.join(f'{k}: {v}' for k, v in mx.items())}}}\")","+    say(f\"violations: {len(violations)}\")","+    for v in violations[:50]:","+        say(v)","+    with open(f\"{HERE}/summary.json\", \"w\") as fh:","+        json.dump({\"per_n\": per_n, \"total\": dict(total), \"mx\": {k: str(v) for k, v in mx.items()},","+                   \"mx_per_n\": mx_per_n,","+                   \"pin\": {\"graphs\": len(pin_rows), \"ok\": pin_ok, \"worst_deficit\": worst[\"deficit\"],","+                           \"worst_n\": worst[\"n\"], \"cnt\": dict(pin_cnt),","+                           \"mx\": {k: str(v) for k, v in pin_mx.items()}},","+                   \"violations\": len(violations), \"seconds\": round(time.time() - t0, 1)}, fh, indent=1)","+    say(\"OK\" if not violations else \"VIOLATIONS\")","+","+","+if __name__ == \"__main__\":","+    main()"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/09_assembly/run.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":14,"lines":["+# item 09 brute-force check, 2026-11-02 05:41:08 UTC, every graph on 1..8 vertices (nauty-geng), 8 workers; 500 random graphs at n ≤ 12 for the pin","+n=1: 1 graphs; IX 2, CM 1, FC 1, BC components 0 (cubic 0, second kind 0), A1 0; maxima {'rho_need_A2': '