d\n\nNote: Use `set_option maxHeartbeats <num>` to set the limit.\n\nHint: Additional diagnostic information may be available using the `set_option diagnostics true` command.\nSome required targets logged failures:\n- MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound.Pathwidth\nerror: build failed\n\nreal\t0m7.106s\nuser\t0m7.198s\nsys\t0m0.729s","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/lean/MOSPFormalization/DegreeBound/Pathwidth.lean","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":390,"lines":["+/-","+Copyright (c) 2026 Alexandre Linhares. All rights reserved.","+Released under the MIT license as described in the file LICENSE.","+","+# The pathwidth assembly: Lemma 5.1 and Corollary 5.2 of Edwards & McDermid (2015), conditional on","+two named hypotheses","+","+Item 09 of loop0012 (`reports/edwards_mcdermid_plan.md` §0.3, §0.5; `reports/edwards_mcdermid.md`","+§2.6 and §9). This file closes the development: the degree-sequence upper bound on pathwidth,","+","+  `pw(G) ≤ f⁻(G) + τ(n) + 2 ρ(n) + 1`               for every `G` with every degree `0` or `≥ 3`,","+  `pw(G) ≤ Σ_v g(deg_B(v)) + τ(n) + 3 ρ(n) + 1`     for every `G` and every reduced reduct `B` of `G`,","+  `pw(G) ≤ Σ_v g(deg_G(v)) + τ(n) + 3 ρ(n) + 1`     for every `G`,","+","+is proved from Theorem 3.2 (`exists_reduction_set`, item 08) and the graph lemmas of the","+repository, **conditional on two cited results that are stated as named `Prop`s and never","+asserted**:","+","+* `CubicPathwidthBound τ` — **(H1)**, the cubic base case (Fomin & Høie 2006, Theorem 5, as the","+  paper restates it on p. 19: \"there is a function `τ`, with `τ(n) = o(n)`, such that","+  `pw(G) ≤ n/6 − 1/6 + τ(n) + O(log n)`\" for 3-regular `G`);","+* `ReductionPathwidthBound ρ` — **(H3)**, the reduction lemma (Kneis, Mölle, Richter &","+  Rossmanith 2009, as the paper uses it on p. 20: \"`pw(G − X_G) = pw(r(G − X_G)) + O(log n)`\",","+  and \"series-parallel graphs … The pathwidth of these graphs is `O(log n)`\", p. 5).","+","+The paper gives no constants for either (`τ(n) = o(n)`, the `O(log n)` unspecified), so each","+hypothesis is parameterised by a budget `ℕ → ℚ` and every theorem carries the budgets it uses:","+`τ` once (applied to a cubic component on at most `n` vertices, which is where `Monotone τ`","+enters), `ρ` once per use of (H3) — inside a basic component of the second kind (`C − v →* ⊥`),","+for `G − X →* B` in Lemma 5.1, and for `G →* B` in Corollary 5.2 — and `+ 1` for the deleted","+vertex `v` of a second-kind component. The paper's `τ(n) + O(log n)` is this with","+`ρ = O(log n)`. Two side conditions on the budgets are needed and stated: `Monotone τ` (the","+paper: \"We can also assume that `τ` is an increasing function of `n`\") and `0 ≤ τ n` (a cubic","+component may be absent, and then the `τ` term is pure slack); `0 ≤ ρ n` is *derived* from","+(H3) (`ReductionPathwidthBound.nonneg`, by `G →* G` in zero steps on `n` vertices).","+","+* `pathwidth_bot`: `pathwidth ⊥ = 0` (one singleton bag per vertex).","+* `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card`: `pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − X) + |X|`, from","+  `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl` (`TreeBound.lean`) and the embedding","+  `G[Xᶜ] → G − X` (`pathwidth_induce_compl_le_isolateSet`); the one-vertex case","+  `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolate_add_one`.","+* `pathwidth_le_rat_of_forall_connected`: `pathwidth G ≤ b` in `ℚ` as soon as every connected","+  vertex set `C` has `pathwidth G[C] ≤ b` and `0 ≤ b` — `pathwidth_induce_le_of_forall_connected`","+  (`TreeBound.lean`) at `⌊b⌋₊`. The paper's \"`pw(G) = max_i pw(G_i)`\" (\"the fact that we have a","+  maximum rather than a sum here is crucial\").","+* Components: `connected_induce_compFinset`, `degree_induce_compFinset`,","+  `subset_compFinset_of_connected`, `pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le_restrict`,","+  `induce_eq_bot_of_forall_degree_eq_zero`.","+* `pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le`: a non-trivial component `C` of a reduced basic graph has","+  `pathwidth G[C] ≤ compPotential G C + τ n + ρ n + 1` — cubic by (H1) on `G[C]` and","+  `compPotential_cubic` (`|C|/6 − 1/6`, \"this is where we use the negative term\"); second kind by","+  `G[C] ≤ G|C`, one deletion, (H3) to `⊥`, and `compPotential_nonneg`.","+* `pathwidth_basic_le`: for reduced basic `B`, `pathwidth B ≤ f⁻(B) + τ n + ρ n + 1` (the max over","+  the components, each bounded by its own term and `compPotential ≤ f⁻`).","+* `pathwidth_le_of_isReductionSet` and **A1** `pathwidth_le_potentialMinus_of_hypotheses`","+  (**Lemma 5.1**): for reduced `G ≠ ⊥`, `pathwidth G ≤ f⁻(G) + τ n + 2 ρ n + 1`, from T1,","+  `pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − X) + |X|`, (H3) on `G − X →* B` and `pathwidth_basic_le`;","+  `pathwidth_le_potential_of_hypotheses` is the paper's displayed form with `f` in place of `f⁻`.","+* **A2** `pathwidth_le_degreeSum_of_hypotheses` (**Corollary 5.2**): for every `G` and every","+  reduced reduct `B` of `G`, `pathwidth G ≤ Σ_v g (B.degree v) + τ n + 3 ρ n + 1` (no `G ≠ ⊥`","+  needed: if `B = ⊥` the bound is the non-negativity of the budgets);","+  `pathwidth_le_histogram_of_hypotheses`: the same with `G`'s own degree histogram, by R2","+  (`SPReduces.potential_le`, reduction never raises a surviving degree, and `g` is monotone) —","+  the corollary's displayed \"`=`\" is a \"`≤`\" (plan §0.4 (6)).","+","+Every deterministic statement here was checked by brute force in the form proved before it was","+stated (`reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/09_assembly/check.py`: every graph on 1–8 vertices,","+13,598 graphs, every vertex set `X` and every connected vertex set `C`; 500 random graphs at","+`n ≤ 12`; zero violations). What is **not** claimed: (H1) or (H3) themselves, or any value of","+`τ`, `ρ`; Theorem 5.3 (its averaging lemma is Edwards & Farr's); that the budgets are tight.","+-/","+import MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound.ReductionTheorem","+import MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound.CutLemma","+import MOSPFormalization.TreeBound","+import MOSPFormalization.Minor","+","+set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false","+","+namespace MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound","+","+open Finset","+","+universe u","+","+/-! ### The two named hypotheses (cited, never asserted) -/","+","+/-- **(H1) The cubic base case**, a named `Prop` with budget `τ`. Edwards & McDermid 2015, p. 19:","+\"Fomin and Høie [12] showed that a 3-regular graph `G` with `m` edges has pathwidth at most","+`(1/9 + o(1)) m + O(log n) = (1/6 + o(1)) n + O(log n)`. Hence for 3-regular graphs, there is a","+function `τ`, with `τ(n) = o(n)`, such that `pw(G) ≤ n/6 − 1/6 + τ(n) + O(log n)` (the negative","+term is needed below). We can also assume that `τ` is an increasing function of `n`.\" Fomin & Høie","+2006, Theorem 5: \"For any `ε > 0`, there exists an integer `n_ε` such that for every graph `G`","+with maximum vertex degree at most three and with `|V(G)| > n_ε`, `pw(G) ≤ (1/6 + ε)|V(G)|`.\"","+The `O(log n)` of the paper's restatement is folded into `τ`; the paper gives no constants, and","+none is asserted here. -/","+def CubicPathwidthBound (τ : ℕ → ℚ) : Prop :=","+  ∀ (W : Type u) [Fintype W] [DecidableEq W] (G : SimpleGraph W) [DecidableRel G.Adj],","+    G.Connected → (∀ v, G.degree v = 3) →","+      (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ (Fintype.card W : ℚ) / 6 - 1 / 6 + τ (Fintype.card W)","+","+/-- **(H3) The reduction lemma**, a named `Prop` with budget `ρ`: a series-parallel reduction","+sequence raises the pathwidth by at most `ρ(n)`. Edwards & McDermid 2015, p. 20: \"It follows from","+the results of [21] that `pw(G) ≤ |X_G| + pw(G − X_G)` and that","+`pw(G − X_G) = pw(r(G − X_G)) + O(log n)`\"; and p. 5: \"series-parallel graphs have treewidth at","+most 2. The pathwidth of these graphs is `O(log n)`\" (the case `H = ⊥`). Reference [21] is","+Kneis, Mölle, Richter & Rossmanith, *SIAM J. Discrete Math.* 23(1):407–427, 2009, which is not","+held (`literature/MISSING.md`). The direction `pw(H) ≤ pw(G)` is unconditional (`r(G)` is a","+minor of `G`) and not needed. -/","+def ReductionPathwidthBound (ρ : ℕ → ℚ) : Prop :=","+  ∀ (W : Type u) [Fintype W] [DecidableEq W] (G H : SimpleGraph W),","+    SPReduces G H → (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ pathwidth H + ρ (Fintype.card W)","+","+/-- (H3) forces a non-negative budget: `G →* G` in zero steps on `n` vertices. -/","+theorem ReductionPathwidthBound.nonneg {ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (n : ℕ) :","+    0 ≤ ρ n := by","+  have := h (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) ⊥ ⊥ (SPReduces.refl _)","+  rw [Fintype.card_ulift, Fintype.card_fin] at this","+  linarith","+","+variable {V : Type u} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]","+","+/-! ### Graph lemmas: the edgeless graph, deleting a vertex set, the maximum over components -/","+","+/-- The edgeless graph has pathwidth `0`: one singleton bag per vertex. -/","+theorem pathwidth_bot : pathwidth (⊥ : SimpleGraph V) = 0 := by","+  apply Nat.eq_zero_of_le_zero","+  let e := Fintype.equivFin V","+  let P : PathDecomposition (⊥ : SimpleGraph V) :=","+    { length := Fintype.card V","+      bag := fun i => univ.filter (fun v => (e v : ℕ) = i.val)","+      vertex_coverage := fun v => ⟨⟨e v, Nat.lt_succ_of_lt (e v).isLt⟩, by simp⟩","+      edge_coverage := fun _ _ h => ((SimpleGraph.bot_adj _ _).1 h).elim","+      interval := fun v i j k hij hjk hi hk => by","+        simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and] at hi hk ⊢","+        have h1 : i.val ≤ j.val := hij","+        have h2 : j.val ≤ k.val := hjk","+        omega }","+  refine (pathwidth_le_width _ P).trans (PathDecomposition.width_le_of_forall_card_le P ?_)","+  intro i","+  show (univ.filter (fun v => (e v : ℕ) = i.val)).card ≤ 0 + 1","+  rw [zero_add]","+  refine card_le_one.2 (fun a ha b hb => e.injective (Fin.ext ?_))","+  simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and] at ha hb","+  omega","+","+/-- `G[Xᶜ]` embeds in `G − X` (the vertices of `X` are isolated there). -/","+theorem pathwidth_induce_compl_le_isolateSet (G : SimpleGraph V) (X : Finset V) :","+    pathwidth (G.induce (↑(Xᶜ) : Set V)) ≤ pathwidth (isolateSet G X) :=","+  pathwidth_le_of_injective","+    (⟨Subtype.val, fun {a b} h =>","+      ⟨h, Finset.mem_compl.1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 a.2), Finset.mem_compl.1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 b.2)⟩⟩ :","+      G.induce (↑(Xᶜ) : Set V) →g isolateSet G X) Subtype.val_injective","+","+/-- **Deleting a vertex set costs at most its size**: `pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − X) + |X|`","+(the paper's \"`pw(G) ≤ |X_G| + pw(G − X_G)`\", which it attributes to [21]; here it is","+`pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl` of `TreeBound.lean`). -/","+theorem pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card (G : SimpleGraph V) (X : Finset V) :","+    pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (isolateSet G X) + X.card := by","+  have h := pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl G Xᶜ","+  rw [compl_compl] at h","+  exact h.trans (Nat.add_le_add_right (pathwidth_induce_compl_le_isolateSet G X) _)","+","+/-- `pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − w) + 1`. -/","+theorem pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolate_add_one (G : SimpleGraph V) (w : V) :","+    pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (isolate G w) + 1 := by","+  have h := pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card G {w}","+  rwa [isolateSet_singleton, card_singleton] at h","+","+/-- **The maximum over components, in `ℚ`**: if every connected vertex set `C` has","+`pathwidth G[C] ≤ b` and `0 ≤ b`, then `pathwidth G ≤ b`. The paper's","+\"`pw(G) = max_i pw(G_i)` (Note that the fact that we have a maximum rather than a sum here is","+crucial.)\" -/","+theorem pathwidth_le_rat_of_forall_connected (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] {b : ℚ}","+    (hb : 0 ≤ b)","+    (h : ∀ C : Finset V, (G.induce (↑C : Set V)).Connected →","+      (pathwidth (G.induce (↑C : Set V)) : ℚ) ≤ b) :","+    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ b := by","+  have hk : pathwidth G ≤ ⌊b⌋₊ := by","+    rw [← pathwidth_induce_univ G]","+    exact pathwidth_induce_le_of_forall_connected G univ ⌊b⌋₊","+      (fun C _ hc => Nat.le_floor (h C hc))","+  calc (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ (⌊b⌋₊ : ℚ) := by exact_mod_cast hk","+    _ ≤ b := Nat.floor_le hb","+","+/-! ### Components of a graph on `V`, as induced subgraphs -/","+","+section Components","+","+variable (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]","+","+theorem coe_compFinset (C : G.ConnectedComponent) : (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V) = C.supp := by","+  ext v","+  exact mem_compFinset_iff_mem_supp G","+","+/-- The induced subgraph on a component is connected. -/","+theorem connected_induce_compFinset (C : G.ConnectedComponent) :","+    (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)).Connected := by","+  rw [coe_compFinset]","+  exact (SimpleGraph.ConnectedComponent.maximal_connected_induce_supp C).1","+","+/-- Degrees inside a component are the degrees in `G` (every neighbour lies in the component). -/","+theorem degree_induce_compFinset {C : G.ConnectedComponent}","+    (v : ↥(↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)) :","+    (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)).degree v = G.degree v := by","+  apply SimpleGraph.degree_induce_of_neighborSet_subset","+  intro u hu","+  rw [SimpleGraph.mem_neighborSet] at hu","+  exact insert_neighborFinset_subset_compFinset G (Finset.mem_coe.1 v.2)","+    (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem ((SimpleGraph.mem_neighborFinset G v u).2 hu))","+","+/-- A connected vertex set lies inside the component of any of its vertices. -/","+theorem subset_compFinset_of_connected {C : Finset V} (hc : (G.induce (↑C : Set V)).Connected)","+    {v : V} (hv : v ∈ C) : C ⊆ compFinset G (G.connectedComponentMk v) := by","+  intro u hu","+  rw [mem_compFinset_mk]","+  have := hc.preconnected ⟨u, Finset.mem_coe.2 hu⟩ ⟨v, Finset.mem_coe.2 hv⟩","+  exact this.map (SimpleGraph.Embedding.induce (↑C : Set V)).toHom","+","+/-- `G[C]` embeds in `G|C` (the restriction on `V`, every other vertex isolated). -/","+theorem pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le_restrict (C : G.ConnectedComponent) :","+    pathwidth (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)) ≤ pathwidth (restrict G C.supp) :=","+  pathwidth_le_of_injective","+    (⟨Subtype.val, fun {a b} h =>","+      ⟨h, (mem_compFinset_iff_mem_supp G).1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 a.2),","+        (mem_compFinset_iff_mem_supp G).1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 b.2)⟩⟩ :","+      G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V) →g restrict G C.supp) Subtype.val_injective","+","+/-- A vertex set of isolated vertices induces the edgeless graph. -/","+theorem induce_eq_bot_of_forall_degree_eq_zero {C : Finset V} (h : ∀ v ∈ C, G.degree v = 0) :","+    G.induce (↑C : Set V) = ⊥ := by","+  ext a b","+  constructor","+  · intro hab","+    have hpos : 0 < G.degree a := (G.degree_pos_iff_exists_adj a).2 ⟨b, hab⟩","+    have := h a (Finset.mem_coe.1 a.2)","+    omega","+  · intro h","+    exact ((SimpleGraph.bot_adj _ _).1 h).elim","+","+/-- `compPotential G C ≤ f⁻(G)`: every other component contributes `≥ 0`. -/","+theorem compPotential_le_potentialMinus (C : G.ConnectedComponent) :","+    compPotential G C ≤ potentialMinus G := by","+  rw [potentialMinus_eq_sum_compPotential]","+  exact single_le_sum (fun D _ => compPotential_nonneg G D) (mem_univ C)","+","+end Components","+","+/-! ### Lemma 5.1: basic graphs, then every reduced graph -/","+","+/-- **The per-component bound** (Lemma 5.1's first paragraph). A non-trivial component `C` of a","+reduced basic graph has `pathwidth G[C] ≤ compPotential G C + τ n + ρ n + 1`: if cubic, by (H1)","+on `G[C]` with `compPotential G C = |C|/6 − 1/6` (\"this is where we use the negative term\") and","+`τ |C| ≤ τ n`; if of the second kind, `G[C]` embeds in `G|C`, deleting `u` costs one, and (H3)","+takes `(G|C) − u →* ⊥` to `pathwidth ⊥ = 0`, so `pathwidth G[C] ≤ ρ n + 1 ≤ compPotential G C +","+τ n + ρ n + 1`. -/","+theorem pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)","+    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)","+    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (hb : IsBasic G) {C : G.ConnectedComponent} {v : V}","+    (hv : v ∈ compFinset G C) (hpos : 0 < G.degree v) :","+    (pathwidth (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)) : ℚ) ≤","+      compPotential G C + τ (Fintype.card V) + ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by","+  have hρ := h3.nonneg (Fintype.card V)","+  rcases isBasic_component G hb hv hpos with hcub | ⟨u, _, hred⟩","+  · -- cubic: (H1) on the component","+    have hc := h1 _ (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)) (connected_induce_compFinset G C)","+      (fun w => by rw [degree_induce_compFinset]; exact hcub w (Finset.mem_coe.1 w.2))","+    simp only [Finset.coe_sort_coe, Fintype.card_coe] at hc","+    rw [compPotential_cubic G hcub]","+    have hmono : τ (compFinset G C).card ≤ τ (Fintype.card V) := hτ (Finset.card_le_univ _)","+    linarith","+  · -- second kind: one deletion, then (H3) to `⊥`","+    have h₁ := pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le_restrict G C","+    have h₂ := pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolate_add_one (restrict G C.supp) u","+    have h₃ := h3 V _ _ hred","+    rw [pathwidth_bot] at h₃","+    have h₄ := compPotential_nonneg G C","+    have hτn := hτ0 (Fintype.card V)","+    have h₅ : (pathwidth (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)) : ℚ) ≤","+        (pathwidth (isolate (restrict G C.supp) u) : ℚ) + 1 := by","+      exact_mod_cast h₁.trans h₂","+    push_cast at h₃","+    linarith","+","+/-- **Lemma 5.1 for basic graphs**: `pathwidth B ≤ f⁻(B) + τ n + ρ n + 1` for every reduced basic","+`B` (the maximum over the components; a connected vertex set with an edge lies in a non-trivial","+component, and one without edges induces `⊥`). -/","+theorem pathwidth_basic_le {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)","+    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)","+    (B : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel B.Adj] (hb : IsBasic B) :","+    (pathwidth B : ℚ) ≤ potentialMinus B + τ (Fintype.card V) + ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by","+  have hρ := h3.nonneg (Fintype.card V)","+  have hτn := hτ0 (Fintype.card V)","+  have hf := potentialMinus_nonneg B","+  refine pathwidth_le_rat_of_forall_connected B (by linarith) (fun C hc => ?_)","+  by_cases hdeg : ∀ v ∈ C, B.degree v = 0","+  · rw [induce_eq_bot_of_forall_degree_eq_zero B hdeg, pathwidth_bot]","+    push_cast","+    linarith","+  · push Not at hdeg","+    obtain ⟨v, hv, hv0⟩ := hdeg","+    have hpos : 0 < B.degree v := Nat.pos_of_ne_zero hv0","+    have hmono := pathwidth_induce_mono B (subset_compFinset_of_connected B hc hv)","+    have hcomp := pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le h1 h3 hτ hτ0 B hb (self_mem_compFinset B v) hpos","+    have hle := compPotential_le_potentialMinus B (B.connectedComponentMk v)","+    have hmono' : (pathwidth (B.induce (↑C : Set V)) : ℚ) ≤","+        pathwidth (B.induce (↑(compFinset B (B.connectedComponentMk v)) : Set V)) := by","+      exact_mod_cast hmono","+    linarith","+","+/-- The assembly for any reduction set (Theorem 3.2's conclusion):","+`pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − X) + |X| ≤ pathwidth B + ρ n + |X| ≤ f⁻(B) + |X| + τ n + 2 ρ n + 1","+≤ f⁻(G) + τ n + 2 ρ n + 1`. -/","+theorem pathwidth_le_of_isReductionSet {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)","+    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)","+    {G B : SimpleGraph V} [DecidableRel G.Adj] [DecidableRel B.Adj] {X : Finset V}","+    (h : IsReductionSet G X B) :","+    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ potentialMinus G + τ (Fintype.card V) + 2 * ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by","+  have hX : (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ pathwidth (isolateSet G X) + X.card := by","+    exact_mod_cast pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card G X","+  have hred := h3 V _ _ h.reduces","+  have hbasic := pathwidth_basic_le h1 h3 hτ hτ0 B h.basic","+  have hcard := h.card_add_le","+  linarith","+","+/-- **A1, Lemma 5.1** (Edwards & McDermid 2015, p. 19, the form its proof establishes): for every","+`G` with every degree `0` or `≥ 3` and at least one edge,","+`pathwidth G ≤ f⁻(G) + τ n + 2 ρ n + 1`, conditional on (H1) with a monotone non-negative","+budget `τ` and on (H3) with budget `ρ`. -/","+theorem pathwidth_le_potentialMinus_of_hypotheses {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)","+    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)","+    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (hG : IsSPReduced G) (hne : G ≠ ⊥) :","+    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ potentialMinus G + τ (Fintype.card V) + 2 * ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by","+  obtain ⟨X, B, instB, h⟩ := exists_reduction_set G hG hne","+  exact pathwidth_le_of_isReductionSet h1 h3 hτ hτ0 h","+","+/-- **Lemma 5.1 as displayed**: `pathwidth G ≤ Σ_v g(deg v) + τ n + 2 ρ n + 1` for reduced","+`G ≠ ⊥` (`f⁻ ≤ f`). -/","+theorem pathwidth_le_potential_of_hypotheses {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)","+    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)","+    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (hG : IsSPReduced G) (hne : G ≠ ⊥) :","+    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤","+      ∑ v, g (G.degree v) + τ (Fintype.card V) + 2 * ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by","+  have h := pathwidth_le_potentialMinus_of_hypotheses h1 h3 hτ hτ0 G hG hne","+  have h' := potentialMinus_le_potential G","+  unfold potential at h'","+  linarith","+","+/-! ### Corollary 5.2 -/","+","+/-- **A2, Corollary 5.2** (Edwards & McDermid 2015, p. 20): for every `G` and every reduced","+reduct `B` of `G` (the paper's `r(G)`),","+`pathwidth G ≤ Σ_v g(deg_B v) + τ n + 3 ρ n + 1`, conditional on (H1) with a monotone","+non-negative budget `τ` and on (H3) with budget `ρ`. No `G ≠ ⊥` is needed: when `B = ⊥` the","+bound is the non-negativity of the budgets. -/","+theorem pathwidth_le_degreeSum_of_hypotheses {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)","+    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)","+    (G : SimpleGraph V) {B : SimpleGraph V} [DecidableRel B.Adj] (hGB : SPReduces G B)","+    (hB : IsSPReduced B) :","+    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤","+      ∑ v, g (B.degree v) + τ (Fintype.card V) + 3 * ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by","+  have hρ := h3.nonneg (Fintype.card V)","+  have hτn := hτ0 (Fintype.card V)","+  have hred := h3 V _ _ hGB","+  have hpot : potentialMinus B ≤ potential B := potentialMinus_le_potential B","+  have hp0 : 0 ≤ potential B := potential_nonneg B","+  have hsum : potential B = ∑ v, g (B.degree v) := rfl","+  by_cases hne : B = ⊥","+  · subst hne","+    rw [pathwidth_bot] at hred","+    push_cast at hred","+    linarith","+  · have hA1 := pathwidth_le_potentialMinus_of_hypotheses h1 h3 hτ hτ0 B hB hne","+    linarith","+","+/-- **Corollary 5.2 with `G`'s own degree histogram**: `pathwidth G ≤ Σ_v g(deg_G v) + τ n +","+3 ρ n + 1` for every `G`, since reduction never raises a surviving degree and `g` is monotone","+(R2, `SPReduces.potential_le`). The paper's displayed \"`=`\" is this \"`≤`\". -/","+theorem pathwidth_le_histogram_of_hypotheses {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)","+    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)","+    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :","+    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤","+      ∑ v, g (G.degree v) + τ (Fintype.card V) + 3 * ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by","+  classical","+  obtain ⟨B, hGB, hB⟩ := exists_reduced_reduct G","+  have h := pathwidth_le_degreeSum_of_hypotheses h1 h3 hτ hτ0 G hGB hB","+  have hle : potential B ≤ potential G := SPReduces.potential_le hGB","+  unfold potential at hle","+  linarith","+","+end MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/Ralph_Loops/loop0012/session_it09.jsonl","hunks":[{"oldStart":462,"oldLines":3,"newStart":462,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5-1\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgda2iecsqX2MwH34HRfo\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":32,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1098,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":242957,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1098,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"6b8bb938-d2d7-4b06-928c-41c6584adc85\",\"uuid\":\"281be4f0-fc84-4437-9f69-bd74259b90f1\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-02T05:44:29.587Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgda2iEpHCX2B2bEjPL67\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":3968,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5-1\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgda2iecsqX2MwH34HRfo\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The names check out (comap decidability instance exists, `Finset.coe_sort_coe`/`Fintype.card_coe` is the card pattern, `Nat.le_floor`/`Nat.floor_le` are the floor lemmas). Writing the Lean file now.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":32,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1098,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":242957,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1098,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"6b8bb938-d2d7-4b06-928c-41c6584adc85\",\"uuid\":\"21b5af34-5376-4530-a85f-7c3c950c6de2\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-02T05:44:29.589Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgda2iEpHCX2B2bEjPL67\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5-1\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgda2iecsqX2MwH34HRfo\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01CwxBMQoYyhtziFziDYA7ez\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cat > /home/al/dev/MOSP/lean/MOSPFormalization/DegreeBound/Pathwidth.lean <<'EOF'\\n/-\\nCopyright (c) 2026 Alexandre Linhares. All rights reserved.\\nReleased under the MIT license as described in the file LICENSE.\\n\\n# The pathwidth assembly: Lemma 5.1 and Corollary 5.2 of Edwards & McDermid (2015), conditional on\\ntwo named hypotheses\\n\\nItem 09 of loop0012 (`reports/edwards_mcdermid_plan.md` §0.3, §0.5; `reports/edwards_mcdermid.md`\\n§2.6 and §9). This file closes the development: the degree-sequence upper bound on pathwidth,\\n\\n  `pw(G) ≤ f⁻(G) + τ(n) + 2 ρ(n) + 1`               for every `G` with every degree `0` or `≥ 3`,\\n  `pw(G) ≤ Σ_v g(deg_B(v)) + τ(n) + 3 ρ(n) + 1`     for every `G` and every reduced reduct `B` of `G`,\\n  `pw(G) ≤ Σ_v g(deg_G(v)) + τ(n) + 3 ρ(n) + 1`     for every `G`,\\n\\nis proved from Theorem 3.2 (`exists_reduction_set`, item 08) and the graph lemmas of the\\nrepository, **conditional on two cited results that are stated as named `Prop`s and never\\nasserted**:\\n\\n* `CubicPathwidthBound τ` — **(H1)**, the cubic base case (Fomin & Høie 2006, Theorem 5, as the\\n  paper restates it on p. 19: \\\"there is a function `τ`, with `τ(n) = o(n)`, such that\\n  `pw(G) ≤ n/6 − 1/6 + τ(n) + O(log n)`\\\" for 3-regular `G`);\\n* `ReductionPathwidthBound ρ` — **(H3)**, the reduction lemma (Kneis, Mölle, Richter &\\n  Rossmanith 2009, as the paper uses it on p. 20: \\\"`pw(G − X_G) = pw(r(G − X_G)) + O(log n)`\\\",\\n  and \\\"series-parallel graphs … The pathwidth of these graphs is `O(log n)`\\\", p. 5).\\n\\nThe paper gives no constants for either (`τ(n) = o(n)`, the `O(log n)` unspecified), so each\\nhypothesis is parameterised by a budget `ℕ → ℚ` and every theorem carries the budgets it uses:\\n`τ` once (applied to a cubic component on at most `n` vertices, which is where `Monotone τ`\\nenters), `ρ` once per use of (H3) — inside a basic component of the second kind (`C − v →* ⊥`),\\nfor `G − X →* B` in Lemma 5.1, and for `G →* B` in Corollary 5.2 — and `+ 1` for the deleted\\nvertex `v` of a second-kind component. The paper's `τ(n) + O(log n)` is this with\\n`ρ = O(log n)`. Two side conditions on the budgets are needed and stated: `Monotone τ` (the\\npaper: \\\"We can also assume that `τ` is an increasing function of `n`\\\") and `0 ≤ τ n` (a cubic\\ncomponent may be absent, and then the `τ` term is pure slack); `0 ≤ ρ n` is *derived* from\\n(H3) (`ReductionPathwidthBound.nonneg`, by `G →* G` in zero steps on `n` vertices).\\n\\n* `pathwidth_bot`: `pathwidth ⊥ = 0` (one singleton bag per vertex).\\n* `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card`: `pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − X) + |X|`, from\\n  `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl` (`TreeBound.lean`) and the embedding\\n  `G[Xᶜ] → G − X` (`pathwidth_induce_compl_le_isolateSet`); the one-vertex case\\n  `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolate_add_one`.\\n* `pathwidth_le_rat_of_forall_connected`: `pathwidth G ≤ b` in `ℚ` as soon as every connected\\n  vertex set `C` has `pathwidth G[C] ≤ b` and `0 ≤ b` — `pathwidth_induce_le_of_forall_connected`\\n  (`TreeBound.lean`) at `⌊b⌋₊`. The paper's \\\"`pw(G) = max_i pw(G_i)`\\\" (\\\"the fact that we have a\\n  maximum rather than a sum here is crucial\\\").\\n* Components: `connected_induce_compFinset`, `degree_induce_compFinset`,\\n  `subset_compFinset_of_connected`, `pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le_restrict`,\\n  `induce_eq_bot_of_forall_degree_eq_zero`.\\n* `pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le`: a non-trivial component `C` of a reduced basic graph has\\n  `pathwidth G[C] ≤ compPotential G C + τ n + ρ n + 1` — cubic by (H1) on `G[C]` and\\n  `compPotential_cubic` (`|C|/6 − 1/6`, \\\"this is where we use the negative term\\\"); second kind by\\n  `G[C] ≤ G|C`, one deletion, (H3) to `⊥`, and `compPotential_nonneg`.\\n* `pathwidth_basic_le`: for reduced basic `B`, `pathwidth B ≤ f⁻(B) + τ n + ρ n + 1` (the max over\\n  the components, each bounded by its own term and `compPotential ≤ f⁻`).\\n* `pathwidth_le_of_isReductionSet` and **A1** `pathwidth_le_potentialMinus_of_hypotheses`\\n  (**Lemma 5.1**): for reduced `G ≠ ⊥`, `pathwidth G ≤ f⁻(G) + τ n + 2 ρ n + 1`, from T1,\\n  `pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − X) + |X|`, (H3) on `G − X →* B` and `pathwidth_basic_le`;\\n  `pathwidth_le_potential_of_hypotheses` is the paper's displayed form with `f` in place of `f⁻`.\\n* **A2** `pathwidth_le_degreeSum_of_hypotheses` (**Corollary 5.2**): for every `G` and every\\n  reduced reduct `B` of `G`, `pathwidth G ≤ Σ_v g (B.degree v) + τ n + 3 ρ n + 1` (no `G ≠ ⊥`\\n  needed: if `B = ⊥` the bound is the non-negativity of the budgets);\\n  `pathwidth_le_histogram_of_hypotheses`: the same with `G`'s own degree histogram, by R2\\n  (`SPReduces.potential_le`, reduction never raises a surviving degree, and `g` is monotone) —\\n  the corollary's displayed \\\"`=`\\\" is a \\\"`≤`\\\" (plan §0.4 (6)).\\n\\nEvery deterministic statement here was checked by brute force in the form proved before it was\\nstated (`reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/09_assembly/check.py`: every graph on 1–8 vertices,\\n13,598 graphs, every vertex set `X` and every connected vertex set `C`; 500 random graphs at\\n`n ≤ 12`; zero violations). What is **not** claimed: (H1) or (H3) themselves, or any value of\\n`τ`, `ρ`; Theorem 5.3 (its averaging lemma is Edwards & Farr's); that the budgets are tight.\\n-/\\nimport MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound.ReductionTheorem\\nimport MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound.CutLemma\\nimport MOSPFormalization.TreeBound\\nimport MOSPFormalization.Minor\\n\\nset_option linter.unusedSectionVars false\\n\\nnamespace MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound\\n\\nopen Finset\\n\\nuniverse u\\n\\n/-! ### The two named hypotheses (cited, never asserted) -/\\n\\n/-- **(H1) The cubic base case**, a named `Prop` with budget `τ`. Edwards & McDermid 2015, p. 19:\\n\\\"Fomin and Høie [12] showed that a 3-regular graph `G` with `m` edges has pathwidth at most\\n`(1/9 + o(1)) m + O(log n) = (1/6 + o(1)) n + O(log n)`. Hence for 3-regular graphs, there is a\\nfunction `τ`, with `τ(n) = o(n)`, such that `pw(G) ≤ n/6 − 1/6 + τ(n) + O(log n)` (the negative\\nterm is needed below). We can also assume that `τ` is an increasing function of `n`.\\\" Fomin & Høie\\n2006, Theorem 5: \\\"For any `ε > 0`, there exists an integer `n_ε` such that for every graph `G`\\nwith maximum vertex degree at most three and with `|V(G)| > n_ε`, `pw(G) ≤ (1/6 + ε)|V(G)|`.\\\"\\nThe `O(log n)` of the paper's restatement is folded into `τ`; the paper gives no constants, and\\nnone is asserted here. -/\\ndef CubicPathwidthBound (τ : ℕ → ℚ) : Prop :=\\n  ∀ (W : Type u) [Fintype W] [DecidableEq W] (G : SimpleGraph W) [DecidableRel G.Adj],\\n    G.Connected → (∀ v, G.degree v = 3) →\\n      (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ (Fintype.card W : ℚ) / 6 - 1 / 6 + τ (Fintype.card W)\\n\\n/-- **(H3) The reduction lemma**, a named `Prop` with budget `ρ`: a series-parallel reduction\\nsequence raises the pathwidth by at most `ρ(n)`. Edwards & McDermid 2015, p. 20: \\\"It follows from\\nthe results of [21] that `pw(G) ≤ |X_G| + pw(G − X_G)` and that\\n`pw(G − X_G) = pw(r(G − X_G)) + O(log n)`\\\"; and p. 5: \\\"series-parallel graphs have treewidth at\\nmost 2. The pathwidth of these graphs is `O(log n)`\\\" (the case `H = ⊥`). Reference [21] is\\nKneis, Mölle, Richter & Rossmanith, *SIAM J. Discrete Math.* 23(1):407–427, 2009, which is not\\nheld (`literature/MISSING.md`). The direction `pw(H) ≤ pw(G)` is unconditional (`r(G)` is a\\nminor of `G`) and not needed. -/\\ndef ReductionPathwidthBound (ρ : ℕ → ℚ) : Prop :=\\n  ∀ (W : Type u) [Fintype W] [DecidableEq W] (G H : SimpleGraph W),\\n    SPReduces G H → (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ pathwidth H + ρ (Fintype.card W)\\n\\n/-- (H3) forces a non-negative budget: `G →* G` in zero steps on `n` vertices. -/\\ntheorem ReductionPathwidthBound.nonneg {ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (n : ℕ) :\\n    0 ≤ ρ n := by\\n  have := h (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) ⊥ ⊥ (SPReduces.refl _)\\n  rw [Fintype.card_ulift, Fintype.card_fin] at this\\n  linarith\\n\\nvariable {V : Type u} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n\\n/-! ### Graph lemmas: the edgeless graph, deleting a vertex set, the maximum over components -/\\n\\n/-- The edgeless graph has pathwidth `0`: one singleton bag per vertex. -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_bot : pathwidth (⊥ : SimpleGraph V) = 0 := by\\n  apply Nat.eq_zero_of_le_zero\\n  let e := Fintype.equivFin V\\n  let P : PathDecomposition (⊥ : SimpleGraph V) :=\\n    { length := Fintype.card V\\n      bag := fun i => univ.filter (fun v => (e v : ℕ) = i.val)\\n      vertex_coverage := fun v => ⟨⟨e v, Nat.lt_succ_of_lt (e v).isLt⟩, by simp⟩\\n      edge_coverage := fun _ _ h => ((SimpleGraph.bot_adj _ _).1 h).elim\\n      interval := fun v i j k hij hjk hi hk => by\\n        simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and] at hi hk ⊢\\n        have h1 : i.val ≤ j.val := hij\\n        have h2 : j.val ≤ k.val := hjk\\n        omega }\\n  refine (pathwidth_le_width _ P).trans (PathDecomposition.width_le_of_forall_card_le P ?_)\\n  intro i\\n  show (univ.filter (fun v => (e v : ℕ) = i.val)).card ≤ 0 + 1\\n  rw [zero_add]\\n  refine card_le_one.2 (fun a ha b hb => e.injective (Fin.ext ?_))\\n  simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and] at ha hb\\n  omega\\n\\n/-- `G[Xᶜ]` embeds in `G − X` (the vertices of `X` are isolated there). -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_compl_le_isolateSet (G : SimpleGraph V) (X : Finset V) :\\n    pathwidth (G.induce (↑(Xᶜ) : Set V)) ≤ pathwidth (isolateSet G X) :=\\n  pathwidth_le_of_injective\\n    (⟨Subtype.val, fun {a b} h =>\\n      ⟨h, Finset.mem_compl.1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 a.2), Finset.mem_compl.1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 b.2)⟩⟩ :\\n      G.induce (↑(Xᶜ) : Set V) →g isolateSet G X) Subtype.val_injective\\n\\n/-- **Deleting a vertex set costs at most its size**: `pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − X) + |X|`\\n(the paper's \\\"`pw(G) ≤ |X_G| + pw(G − X_G)`\\\", which it attributes to [21]; here it is\\n`pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl` of `TreeBound.lean`). -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card (G : SimpleGraph V) (X : Finset V) :\\n    pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (isolateSet G X) + X.card := by\\n  have h := pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl G Xᶜ\\n  rw [compl_compl] at h\\n  exact h.trans (Nat.add_le_add_right (pathwidth_induce_compl_le_isolateSet G X) _)\\n\\n/-- `pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − w) + 1`. -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolate_add_one (G : SimpleGraph V) (w : V) :\\n    pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (isolate G w) + 1 := by\\n  have h := pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card G {w}\\n  rwa [isolateSet_singleton, card_singleton] at h\\n\\n/-- **The maximum over components, in `ℚ`**: if every connected vertex set `C` has\\n`pathwidth G[C] ≤ b` and `0 ≤ b`, then `pathwidth G ≤ b`. The paper's\\n\\\"`pw(G) = max_i pw(G_i)` (Note that the fact that we have a maximum rather than a sum here is\\ncrucial.)\\\" -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_le_rat_of_forall_connected (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] {b : ℚ}\\n    (hb : 0 ≤ b)\\n    (h : ∀ C : Finset V, (G.induce (↑C : Set V)).Connected →\\n      (pathwidth (G.induce (↑C : Set V)) : ℚ) ≤ b) :\\n    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ b := by\\n  have hk : pathwidth G ≤ ⌊b⌋₊ := by\\n    rw [← pathwidth_induce_univ G]\\n    exact pathwidth_induce_le_of_forall_connected G univ ⌊b⌋₊\\n      (fun C _ hc => Nat.le_floor (h C hc))\\n  calc (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ (⌊b⌋₊ : ℚ) := by exact_mod_cast hk\\n    _ ≤ b := Nat.floor_le hb\\n\\n/-! ### Components of a graph on `V`, as induced subgraphs -/\\n\\nsection Components\\n\\nvariable (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n\\ntheorem coe_compFinset (C : G.ConnectedComponent) : (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V) = C.supp := by\\n  ext v\\n  exact mem_compFinset_iff_mem_supp G\\n\\n/-- The induced subgraph on a component is connected. -/\\ntheorem connected_induce_compFinset (C : G.ConnectedComponent) :\\n    (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)).Connected := by\\n  rw [coe_compFinset]\\n  exact (SimpleGraph.ConnectedComponent.maximal_connected_induce_supp C).1\\n\\n/-- Degrees inside a component are the degrees in `G` (every neighbour lies in the component). -/\\ntheorem degree_induce_compFinset {C : G.ConnectedComponent}\\n    (v : ↥(↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)) :\\n    (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)).degree v = G.degree v := by\\n  apply SimpleGraph.degree_induce_of_neighborSet_subset\\n  intro u hu\\n  rw [SimpleGraph.mem_neighborSet] at hu\\n  exact insert_neighborFinset_subset_compFinset G (Finset.mem_coe.1 v.2)\\n    (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem ((SimpleGraph.mem_neighborFinset G v u).2 hu))\\n\\n/-- A connected vertex set lies inside the component of any of its vertices. -/\\ntheorem subset_compFinset_of_connected {C : Finset V} (hc : (G.induce (↑C : Set V)).Connected)\\n    {v : V} (hv : v ∈ C) : C ⊆ compFinset G (G.connectedComponentMk v) := by\\n  intro u hu\\n  rw [mem_compFinset_mk]\\n  have := hc.preconnected ⟨u, Finset.mem_coe.2 hu⟩ ⟨v, Finset.mem_coe.2 hv⟩\\n  exact this.map (SimpleGraph.Embedding.induce (↑C : Set V)).toHom\\n\\n/-- `G[C]` embeds in `G|C` (the restriction on `V`, every other vertex isolated). -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le_restrict (C : G.ConnectedComponent) :\\n    pathwidth (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)) ≤ pathwidth (restrict G C.supp) :=\\n  pathwidth_le_of_injective\\n    (⟨Subtype.val, fun {a b} h =>\\n      ⟨h, (mem_compFinset_iff_mem_supp G).1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 a.2),\\n        (mem_compFinset_iff_mem_supp G).1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 b.2)⟩⟩ :\\n      G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V) →g restrict G C.supp) Subtype.val_injective\\n\\n/-- A vertex set of isolated vertices induces the edgeless graph. -/\\ntheorem induce_eq_bot_of_forall_degree_eq_zero {C : Finset V} (h : ∀ v ∈ C, G.degree v = 0) :\\n    G.induce (↑C : Set V) = ⊥ := by\\n  ext a b\\n  constructor\\n  · intro hab\\n    have hpos : 0 < G.degree a := (G.degree_pos_iff_exists_adj a).2 ⟨b, hab⟩\\n    have := h a (Finset.mem_coe.1 a.2)\\n    omega\\n  · intro h\\n    exact ((SimpleGraph.bot_adj _ _).1 h).elim\\n\\n/-- `compPotential G C ≤ f⁻(G)`: every other component contributes `≥ 0`. -/\\ntheorem compPotential_le_potentialMinus (C : G.ConnectedComponent) :\\n    compPotential G C ≤ potentialMinus G := by\\n  rw [potentialMinus_eq_sum_compPotential]\\n  exact single_le_sum (fun D _ => compPotential_nonneg G D) (mem_univ C)\\n\\nend Components\\n\\n/-! ### Lemma 5.1: basic graphs, then every reduced graph -/\\n\\n/-- **The per-component bound** (Lemma 5.1's first paragraph). A non-trivial component `C` of a\\nreduced basic graph has `pathwidth G[C] ≤ compPotential G C + τ n + ρ n + 1`: if cubic, by (H1)\\non `G[C]` with `compPotential G C = |C|/6 − 1/6` (\\\"this is where we use the negative term\\\") and\\n`τ |C| ≤ τ n`; if of the second kind, `G[C]` embeds in `G|C`, deleting `u` costs one, and (H3)\\ntakes `(G|C) − u →* ⊥` to `pathwidth ⊥ = 0`, so `pathwidth G[C] ≤ ρ n + 1 ≤ compPotential G C +\\nτ n + ρ n + 1`. -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)\\n    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (hb : IsBasic G) {C : G.ConnectedComponent} {v : V}\\n    (hv : v ∈ compFinset G C) (hpos : 0 < G.degree v) :\\n    (pathwidth (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)) : ℚ) ≤\\n      compPotential G C + τ (Fintype.card V) + ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by\\n  have hρ := h3.nonneg (Fintype.card V)\\n  rcases isBasic_component G hb hv hpos with hcub | ⟨u, _, hred⟩\\n  · -- cubic: (H1) on the component\\n    have hc := h1 _ (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)) (connected_induce_compFinset G C)\\n      (fun w => by rw [degree_induce_compFinset]; exact hcub w (Finset.mem_coe.1 w.2))\\n    simp only [Finset.coe_sort_coe, Fintype.card_coe] at hc\\n    rw [compPotential_cubic G hcub]\\n    have hmono : τ (compFinset G C).card ≤ τ (Fintype.card V) := hτ (Finset.card_le_univ _)\\n    linarith\\n  · -- second kind: one deletion, then (H3) to `⊥`\\n    have h₁ := pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le_restrict G C\\n    have h₂ := pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolate_add_one (restrict G C.supp) u\\n    have h₃ := h3 V _ _ hred\\n    rw [pathwidth_bot] at h₃\\n    have h₄ := compPotential_nonneg G C\\n    have hτn := hτ0 (Fintype.card V)\\n    have h₅ : (pathwidth (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)) : ℚ) ≤\\n        (pathwidth (isolate (restrict G C.supp) u) : ℚ) + 1 := by\\n      exact_mod_cast h₁.trans h₂\\n    push_cast at h₃\\n    linarith\\n\\n/-- **Lemma 5.1 for basic graphs**: `pathwidth B ≤ f⁻(B) + τ n + ρ n + 1` for every reduced basic\\n`B` (the maximum over the components; a connected vertex set with an edge lies in a non-trivial\\ncomponent, and one without edges induces `⊥`). -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_basic_le {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)\\n    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)\\n    (B : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel B.Adj] (hb : IsBasic B) :\\n    (pathwidth B : ℚ) ≤ potentialMinus B + τ (Fintype.card V) + ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by\\n  have hρ := h3.nonneg (Fintype.card V)\\n  have hτn := hτ0 (Fintype.card V)\\n  have hf := potentialMinus_nonneg B\\n  refine pathwidth_le_rat_of_forall_connected B (by linarith) (fun C hc => ?_)\\n  by_cases hdeg : ∀ v ∈ C, B.degree v = 0\\n  · rw [induce_eq_bot_of_forall_degree_eq_zero B hdeg, pathwidth_bot]\\n    push_cast\\n    linarith\\n  · push Not at hdeg\\n    obtain ⟨v, hv, hv0⟩ := hdeg\\n    have hpos : 0 < B.degree v := Nat.pos_of_ne_zero hv0\\n    have hmono := pathwidth_induce_mono B (subset_compFinset_of_connected B hc hv)\\n    have hcomp := pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le h1 h3 hτ hτ0 B hb (self_mem_compFinset B v) hpos\\n    have hle := compPotential_le_potentialMinus B (B.connectedComponentMk v)\\n    have hmono' : (pathwidth (B.induce (↑C : Set V)) : ℚ) ≤\\n        pathwidth (B.induce (↑(compFinset B (B.connectedComponentMk v)) : Set V)) := by\\n      exact_mod_cast hmono\\n    linarith\\n\\n/-- The assembly for any reduction set (Theorem 3.2's conclusion):\\n`pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − X) + |X| ≤ pathwidth B + ρ n + |X| ≤ f⁻(B) + |X| + τ n + 2 ρ n + 1\\n≤ f⁻(G) + τ n + 2 ρ n + 1`. -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_le_of_isReductionSet {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)\\n    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)\\n    {G B : SimpleGraph V} [DecidableRel G.Adj] [DecidableRel B.Adj] {X : Finset V}\\n    (h : IsReductionSet G X B) :\\n    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ potentialMinus G + τ (Fintype.card V) + 2 * ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by\\n  have hX : (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ pathwidth (isolateSet G X) + X.card := by\\n    exact_mod_cast pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card G X\\n  have hred := h3 V _ _ h.reduces\\n  have hbasic := pathwidth_basic_le h1 h3 hτ hτ0 B h.basic\\n  have hcard := h.card_add_le\\n  linarith\\n\\n/-- **A1, Lemma 5.1** (Edwards & McDermid 2015, p. 19, the form its proof establishes): for every\\n`G` with every degree `0` or `≥ 3` and at least one edge,\\n`pathwidth G ≤ f⁻(G) + τ n + 2 ρ n + 1`, conditional on (H1) with a monotone non-negative\\nbudget `τ` and on (H3) with budget `ρ`. -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_le_potentialMinus_of_hypotheses {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)\\n    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (hG : IsSPReduced G) (hne : G ≠ ⊥) :\\n    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ potentialMinus G + τ (Fintype.card V) + 2 * ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by\\n  obtain ⟨X, B, instB, h⟩ := exists_reduction_set G hG hne\\n  exact pathwidth_le_of_isReductionSet h1 h3 hτ hτ0 h\\n\\n/-- **Lemma 5.1 as displayed**: `pathwidth G ≤ Σ_v g(deg v) + τ n + 2 ρ n + 1` for reduced\\n`G ≠ ⊥` (`f⁻ ≤ f`). -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_le_potential_of_hypotheses {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)\\n    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (hG : IsSPReduced G) (hne : G ≠ ⊥) :\\n    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤\\n      ∑ v, g (G.degree v) + τ (Fintype.card V) + 2 * ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by\\n  have h := pathwidth_le_potentialMinus_of_hypotheses h1 h3 hτ hτ0 G hG hne\\n  have h' := potentialMinus_le_potential G\\n  unfold potential at h'\\n  linarith\\n\\n/-! ### Corollary 5.2 -/\\n\\n/-- **A2, Corollary 5.2** (Edwards & McDermid 2015, p. 20): for every `G` and every reduced\\nreduct `B` of `G` (the paper's `r(G)`),\\n`pathwidth G ≤ Σ_v g(deg_B v) + τ n + 3 ρ n + 1`, conditional on (H1) with a monotone\\nnon-negative budget `τ` and on (H3) with budget `ρ`. No `G ≠ ⊥` is needed: when `B = ⊥` the\\nbound is the non-negativity of the budgets. -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_le_degreeSum_of_hypotheses {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)\\n    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) {B : SimpleGraph V} [DecidableRel B.Adj] (hGB : SPReduces G B)\\n    (hB : IsSPReduced B) :\\n    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤\\n      ∑ v, g (B.degree v) + τ (Fintype.card V) + 3 * ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by\\n  have hρ := h3.nonneg (Fintype.card V)\\n  have hτn := hτ0 (Fintype.card V)\\n  have hred := h3 V _ _ hGB\\n  have hpot : potentialMinus B ≤ potential B := potentialMinus_le_potential B\\n  have hp0 : 0 ≤ potential B := potential_nonneg B\\n  have hsum : potential B = ∑ v, g (B.degree v) := rfl\\n  by_cases hne : B = ⊥\\n  · subst hne\\n    rw [pathwidth_bot] at hred\\n    push_cast at hred\\n    linarith\\n  · have hA1 := pathwidth_le_potentialMinus_of_hypotheses h1 h3 hτ hτ0 B hB hne\\n    linarith\\n\\n/-- **Corollary 5.2 with `G`'s own degree histogram**: `pathwidth G ≤ Σ_v g(deg_G v) + τ n +\\n3 ρ n + 1` for every `G`, since reduction never raises a surviving degree and `g` is monotone\\n(R2, `SPReduces.potential_le`). The paper's displayed \\\"`=`\\\" is this \\\"`≤`\\\". -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_le_histogram_of_hypotheses {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)\\n    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\\n    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤\\n      ∑ v, g (G.degree v) + τ (Fintype.card V) + 3 * ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by\\n  classical\\n  obtain ⟨B, hGB, hB⟩ := exists_reduced_reduct G\\n  have h := pathwidth_le_degreeSum_of_hypotheses h1 h3 hτ hτ0 G hGB hB\\n  have hle : potential B ≤ potential G := SPReduces.potential_le hGB\\n  unfold potential at hle\\n  linarith\\n\\nend MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound\\nEOF\\ncd /home/al/dev/MOSP/lean && time lake build MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound.Pathwidth 2>&1 | tail -60\",\"description\":\"Write Pathwidth.lean and build it\",\"timeout\":900000},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":32,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1098,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":242957,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1098,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"6b8bb938-d2d7-4b06-928c-41c6584adc85\",\"uuid\":\"a0fb0c2d-994f-4aaf-a937-e976a692b515\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-02T05:46:20.958Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgda2iEpHCX2B2bEjPL67\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01CwxBMQoYyhtziFziDYA7ez\":{\"command\":\"cat > /home/al/dev/MOSP/lean/MOSPFormalization/DegreeBound/Pathwidth.lean <<'EOF'\\n/-\\nCopyright (c) 2026 Alexandre Linhares. All rights reserved.\\nReleased under the MIT license as described in the file LICENSE.\\n\\n# The pathwidth assembly: Lemma 5.1 and Corollary 5.2 of Edwards & McDermid (2015), conditional on\\ntwo named hypotheses\\n\\nItem 09 of loop0012 (`reports/edwards_mcdermid_plan.md` §0.3, §0.5; `reports/edwards_mcdermid.md`\\n§2.6 and §9). This file closes the development: the degree-sequence upper bound on pathwidth,\\n\\n  `pw(G) ≤ f⁻(G) + τ(n) + 2 ρ(n) + 1`               for every `G` with every degree `0` or `≥ 3`,\\n  `pw(G) ≤ Σ_v g(deg_B(v)) + τ(n) + 3 ρ(n) + 1`     for every `G` and every reduced reduct `B` of `G`,\\n  `pw(G) ≤ Σ_v g(deg_G(v)) + τ(n) + 3 ρ(n) + 1`     for every `G`,\\n\\nis proved from Theorem 3.2 (`exists_reduction_set`, item 08) and the graph lemmas of the\\nrepository, **conditional on two cited results that are stated as named `Prop`s and never\\nasserted**:\\n\\n* `CubicPathwidthBound τ` — **(H1)**, the cubic base case (Fomin & Høie 2006, Theorem 5, as the\\n  paper restates it on p. 19: \\\"there is a function `τ`, with `τ(n) = o(n)`, such that\\n  `pw(G) ≤ n/6 − 1/6 + τ(n) + O(log n)`\\\" for 3-regular `G`);\\n* `ReductionPathwidthBound ρ` — **(H3)**, the reduction lemma (Kneis, Mölle, Richter &\\n  Rossmanith 2009, as the paper uses it on p. 20: \\\"`pw(G − X_G) = pw(r(G − X_G)) + O(log n)`\\\",\\n  and \\\"series-parallel graphs … The pathwidth of these graphs is `O(log n)`\\\", p. 5).\\n\\nThe paper gives no constants for either (`τ(n) = o(n)`, the `O(log n)` unspecified), so each\\nhypothesis is parameterised by a budget `ℕ → ℚ` and every theorem carries the budgets it uses:\\n`τ` once (applied to a cubic component on at most `n` vertices, which is where `Monotone τ`\\nenters), `ρ` once per use of (H3) — inside a basic component of the second kind (`C − v →* ⊥`),\\nfor `G − X →* B` in Lemma 5.1, and for `G →* B` in Corollary 5.2 — and `+ 1` for the deleted\\nvertex `v` of a second-kind component. The paper's `τ(n) + O(log n)` is this with\\n`ρ = O(log n)`. Two side conditions on the budgets are needed and stated: `Monotone τ` (the\\npaper: \\\"We can also assume that `τ` is an increasing function of `n`\\\") and `0 ≤ τ n` (a cubic\\ncomponent may be absent, and then the `τ` term is pure slack); `0 ≤ ρ n` is *derived* from\\n(H3) (`ReductionPathwidthBound.nonneg`, by `G →* G` in zero steps on `n` vertices).\\n\\n* `pathwidth_bot`: `pathwidth ⊥ = 0` (one singleton bag per vertex).\\n* `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card`: `pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − X) + |X|`, from\\n  `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl` (`TreeBound.lean`) and the embedding\\n  `G[Xᶜ] → G − X` (`pathwidth_induce_compl_le_isolateSet`); the one-vertex case\\n  `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolate_add_one`.\\n* `pathwidth_le_rat_of_forall_connected`: `pathwidth G ≤ b` in `ℚ` as soon as every connected\\n  vertex set `C` has `pathwidth G[C] ≤ b` and `0 ≤ b` — `pathwidth_induce_le_of_forall_connected`\\n  (`TreeBound.lean`) at `⌊b⌋₊`. The paper's \\\"`pw(G) = max_i pw(G_i)`\\\" (\\\"the fact that we have a\\n  maximum rather than a sum here is crucial\\\").\\n* Components: `connected_induce_compFinset`, `degree_induce_compFinset`,\\n  `subset_compFinset_of_connected`, `pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le_restrict`,\\n  `induce_eq_bot_of_forall_degree_eq_zero`.\\n* `pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le`: a non-trivial component `C` of a reduced basic graph has\\n  `pathwidth G[C] ≤ compPotential G C + τ n + ρ n + 1` — cubic by (H1) on `G[C]` and\\n  `compPotential_cubic` (`|C|/6 − 1/6`, \\\"this is where we use the negative term\\\"); second kind by\\n  `G[C] ≤ G|C`, one deletion, (H3) to `⊥`, and `compPotential_nonneg`.\\n* `pathwidth_basic_le`: for reduced basic `B`, `pathwidth B ≤ f⁻(B) + τ n + ρ n + 1` (the max over\\n  the components, each bounded by its own term and `compPotential ≤ f⁻`).\\n* `pathwidth_le_of_isReductionSet` and **A1** `pathwidth_le_potentialMinus_of_hypotheses`\\n  (**Lemma 5.1**): for reduced `G ≠ ⊥`, `pathwidth G ≤ f⁻(G) + τ n + 2 ρ n + 1`, from T1,\\n  `pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − X) + |X|`, (H3) on `G − X →* B` and `pathwidth_basic_le`;\\n  `pathwidth_le_potential_of_hypotheses` is the paper's displayed form with `f` in place of `f⁻`.\\n* **A2** `pathwidth_le_degreeSum_of_hypotheses` (**Corollary 5.2**): for every `G` and every\\n  reduced reduct `B` of `G`, `pathwidth G ≤ Σ_v g (B.degree v) + τ n + 3 ρ n + 1` (no `G ≠ ⊥`\\n  needed: if `B = ⊥` the bound is the non-negativity of the budgets);\\n  `pathwidth_le_histogram_of_hypotheses`: the same with `G`'s own degree histogram, by R2\\n  (`SPReduces.potential_le`, reduction never raises a surviving degree, and `g` is monotone) —\\n  the corollary's displayed \\\"`=`\\\" is a \\\"`≤`\\\" (plan §0.4 (6)).\\n\\nEvery deterministic statement here was checked by brute force in the form proved before it was\\nstated (`reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/09_assembly/check.py`: every graph on 1–8 vertices,\\n13,598 graphs, every vertex set `X` and every connected vertex set `C`; 500 random graphs at\\n`n ≤ 12`; zero violations). What is **not** claimed: (H1) or (H3) themselves, or any value of\\n`τ`, `ρ`; Theorem 5.3 (its averaging lemma is Edwards & Farr's); that the budgets are tight.\\n-/\\nimport MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound.ReductionTheorem\\nimport MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound.CutLemma\\nimport MOSPFormalization.TreeBound\\nimport MOSPFormalization.Minor\\n\\nset_option linter.unusedSectionVars false\\n\\nnamespace MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound\\n\\nopen Finset\\n\\nuniverse u\\n\\n/-! ### The two named hypotheses (cited, never asserted) -/\\n\\n/-- **(H1) The cubic base case**, a named `Prop` with budget `τ`. Edwards & McDermid 2015, p. 19:\\n\\\"Fomin and Høie [12] showed that a 3-regular graph `G` with `m` edges has pathwidth at most\\n`(1/9 + o(1)) m + O(log n) = (1/6 + o(1)) n + O(log n)`. Hence for 3-regular graphs, there is a\\nfunction `τ`, with `τ(n) = o(n)`, such that `pw(G) ≤ n/6 − 1/6 + τ(n) + O(log n)` (the negative\\nterm is needed below). We can also assume that `τ` is an increasing function of `n`.\\\" Fomin & Høie\\n2006, Theorem 5: \\\"For any `ε > 0`, there exists an integer `n_ε` such that for every graph `G`\\nwith maximum vertex degree at most three and with `|V(G)| > n_ε`, `pw(G) ≤ (1/6 + ε)|V(G)|`.\\\"\\nThe `O(log n)` of the paper's restatement is folded into `τ`; the paper gives no constants, and\\nnone is asserted here. -/\\ndef CubicPathwidthBound (τ : ℕ → ℚ) : Prop :=\\n  ∀ (W : Type u) [Fintype W] [DecidableEq W] (G : SimpleGraph W) [DecidableRel G.Adj],\\n    G.Connected → (∀ v, G.degree v = 3) →\\n      (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ (Fintype.card W : ℚ) / 6 - 1 / 6 + τ (Fintype.card W)\\n\\n/-- **(H3) The reduction lemma**, a named `Prop` with budget `ρ`: a series-parallel reduction\\nsequence raises the pathwidth by at most `ρ(n)`. Edwards & McDermid 2015, p. 20: \\\"It follows from\\nthe results of [21] that `pw(G) ≤ |X_G| + pw(G − X_G)` and that\\n`pw(G − X_G) = pw(r(G − X_G)) + O(log n)`\\\"; and p. 5: \\\"series-parallel graphs have treewidth at\\nmost 2. The pathwidth of these graphs is `O(log n)`\\\" (the case `H = ⊥`). Reference [21] is\\nKneis, Mölle, Richter & Rossmanith, *SIAM J. Discrete Math.* 23(1):407–427, 2009, which is not\\nheld (`literature/MISSING.md`). The direction `pw(H) ≤ pw(G)` is unconditional (`r(G)` is a\\nminor of `G`) and not needed. -/\\ndef ReductionPathwidthBound (ρ : ℕ → ℚ) : Prop :=\\n  ∀ (W : Type u) [Fintype W] [DecidableEq W] (G H : SimpleGraph W),\\n    SPReduces G H → (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ pathwidth H + ρ (Fintype.card W)\\n\\n/-- (H3) forces a non-negative budget: `G →* G` in zero steps on `n` vertices. -/\\ntheorem ReductionPathwidthBound.nonneg {ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (n : ℕ) :\\n    0 ≤ ρ n := by\\n  have := h (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) ⊥ ⊥ (SPReduces.refl _)\\n  rw [Fintype.card_ulift, Fintype.card_fin] at this\\n  linarith\\n\\nvariable {V : Type u} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n\\n/-! ### Graph lemmas: the edgeless graph, deleting a vertex set, the maximum over components -/\\n\\n/-- The edgeless graph has pathwidth `0`: one singleton bag per vertex. -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_bot : pathwidth (⊥ : SimpleGraph V) = 0 := by\\n  apply Nat.eq_zero_of_le_zero\\n  let e := Fintype.equivFin V\\n  let P : PathDecomposition (⊥ : SimpleGraph V) :=\\n    { length := Fintype.card V\\n      bag := fun i => univ.filter (fun v => (e v : ℕ) = i.val)\\n      vertex_coverage := fun v => ⟨⟨e v, Nat.lt_succ_of_lt (e v).isLt⟩, by simp⟩\\n      edge_coverage := fun _ _ h => ((SimpleGraph.bot_adj _ _).1 h).elim\\n      interval := fun v i j k hij hjk hi hk => by\\n        simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and] at hi hk ⊢\\n        have h1 : i.val ≤ j.val := hij\\n        have h2 : j.val ≤ k.val := hjk\\n        omega }\\n  refine (pathwidth_le_width _ P).trans (PathDecomposition.width_le_of_forall_card_le P ?_)\\n  intro i\\n  show (univ.filter (fun v => (e v : ℕ) = i.val)).card ≤ 0 + 1\\n  rw [zero_add]\\n  refine card_le_one.2 (fun a ha b hb => e.injective (Fin.ext ?_))\\n  simp only [mem_filter, mem_univ, true_and] at ha hb\\n  omega\\n\\n/-- `G[Xᶜ]` embeds in `G − X` (the vertices of `X` are isolated there). -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_compl_le_isolateSet (G : SimpleGraph V) (X : Finset V) :\\n    pathwidth (G.induce (↑(Xᶜ) : Set V)) ≤ pathwidth (isolateSet G X) :=\\n  pathwidth_le_of_injective\\n    (⟨Subtype.val, fun {a b} h =>\\n      ⟨h, Finset.mem_compl.1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 a.2), Finset.mem_compl.1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 b.2)⟩⟩ :\\n      G.induce (↑(Xᶜ) : Set V) →g isolateSet G X) Subtype.val_injective\\n\\n/-- **Deleting a vertex set costs at most its size**: `pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − X) + |X|`\\n(the paper's \\\"`pw(G) ≤ |X_G| + pw(G − X_G)`\\\", which it attributes to [21]; here it is\\n`pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl` of `TreeBound.lean`). -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card (G : SimpleGraph V) (X : Finset V) :\\n    pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (isolateSet G X) + X.card := by\\n  have h := pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl G Xᶜ\\n  rw [compl_compl] at h\\n  exact h.trans (Nat.add_le_add_right (pathwidth_induce_compl_le_isolateSet G X) _)\\n\\n/-- `pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − w) + 1`. -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolate_add_one (G : SimpleGraph V) (w : V) :\\n    pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (isolate G w) + 1 := by\\n  have h := pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card G {w}\\n  rwa [isolateSet_singleton, card_singleton] at h\\n\\n/-- **The maximum over components, in `ℚ`**: if every connected vertex set `C` has\\n`pathwidth G[C] ≤ b` and `0 ≤ b`, then `pathwidth G ≤ b`. The paper's\\n\\\"`pw(G) = max_i pw(G_i)` (Note that the fact that we have a maximum rather than a sum here is\\ncrucial.)\\\" -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_le_rat_of_forall_connected (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] {b : ℚ}\\n    (hb : 0 ≤ b)\\n    (h : ∀ C : Finset V, (G.induce (↑C : Set V)).Connected →\\n      (pathwidth (G.induce (↑C : Set V)) : ℚ) ≤ b) :\\n    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ b := by\\n  have hk : pathwidth G ≤ ⌊b⌋₊ := by\\n    rw [← pathwidth_induce_univ G]\\n    exact pathwidth_induce_le_of_forall_connected G univ ⌊b⌋₊\\n      (fun C _ hc => Nat.le_floor (h C hc))\\n  calc (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ (⌊b⌋₊ : ℚ) := by exact_mod_cast hk\\n    _ ≤ b := Nat.floor_le hb\\n\\n/-! ### Components of a graph on `V`, as induced subgraphs -/\\n\\nsection Components\\n\\nvariable (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n\\ntheorem coe_compFinset (C : G.ConnectedComponent) : (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V) = C.supp := by\\n  ext v\\n  exact mem_compFinset_iff_mem_supp G\\n\\n/-- The induced subgraph on a component is connected. -/\\ntheorem connected_induce_compFinset (C : G.ConnectedComponent) :\\n    (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)).Connected := by\\n  rw [coe_compFinset]\\n  exact (SimpleGraph.ConnectedComponent.maximal_connected_induce_supp C).1\\n\\n/-- Degrees inside a component are the degrees in `G` (every neighbour lies in the component). -/\\ntheorem degree_induce_compFinset {C : G.ConnectedComponent}\\n    (v : ↥(↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)) :\\n    (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)).degree v = G.degree v := by\\n  apply SimpleGraph.degree_induce_of_neighborSet_subset\\n  intro u hu\\n  rw [SimpleGraph.mem_neighborSet] at hu\\n  exact insert_neighborFinset_subset_compFinset G (Finset.mem_coe.1 v.2)\\n    (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem ((SimpleGraph.mem_neighborFinset G v u).2 hu))\\n\\n/-- A connected vertex set lies inside the component of any of its vertices. -/\\ntheorem subset_compFinset_of_connected {C : Finset V} (hc : (G.induce (↑C : Set V)).Connected)\\n    {v : V} (hv : v ∈ C) : C ⊆ compFinset G (G.connectedComponentMk v) := by\\n  intro u hu\\n  rw [mem_compFinset_mk]\\n  have := hc.preconnected ⟨u, Finset.mem_coe.2 hu⟩ ⟨v, Finset.mem_coe.2 hv⟩\\n  exact this.map (SimpleGraph.Embedding.induce (↑C : Set V)).toHom\\n\\n/-- `G[C]` embeds in `G|C` (the restriction on `V`, every other vertex isolated). -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le_restrict (C : G.ConnectedComponent) :\\n    pathwidth (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)) ≤ pathwidth (restrict G C.supp) :=\\n  pathwidth_le_of_injective\\n    (⟨Subtype.val, fun {a b} h =>\\n      ⟨h, (mem_compFinset_iff_mem_supp G).1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 a.2),\\n        (mem_compFinset_iff_mem_supp G).1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 b.2)⟩⟩ :\\n      G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V) →g restrict G C.supp) Subtype.val_injective\\n\\n/-- A vertex set of isolated vertices induces the edgeless graph. -/\\ntheorem induce_eq_bot_of_forall_degree_eq_zero {C : Finset V} (h : ∀ v ∈ C, G.degree v = 0) :\\n    G.induce (↑C : Set V) = ⊥ := by\\n  ext a b\\n  constructor\\n  · intro hab\\n    have hpos : 0 < G.degree a := (G.degree_pos_iff_exists_adj a).2 ⟨b, hab⟩\\n    have := h a (Finset.mem_coe.1 a.2)\\n    omega\\n  · intro h\\n    exact ((SimpleGraph.bot_adj _ _).1 h).elim\\n\\n/-- `compPotential G C ≤ f⁻(G)`: every other component contributes `≥ 0`. -/\\ntheorem compPotential_le_potentialMinus (C : G.ConnectedComponent) :\\n    compPotential G C ≤ potentialMinus G := by\\n  rw [potentialMinus_eq_sum_compPotential]\\n  exact single_le_sum (fun D _ => compPotential_nonneg G D) (mem_univ C)\\n\\nend Components\\n\\n/-! ### Lemma 5.1: basic graphs, then every reduced graph -/\\n\\n/-- **The per-component bound** (Lemma 5.1's first paragraph). A non-trivial component `C` of a\\nreduced basic graph has `pathwidth G[C] ≤ compPotential G C + τ n + ρ n + 1`: if cubic, by (H1)\\non `G[C]` with `compPotential G C = |C|/6 − 1/6` (\\\"this is where we use the negative term\\\") and\\n`τ |C| ≤ τ n`; if of the second kind, `G[C]` embeds in `G|C`, deleting `u` costs one, and (H3)\\ntakes `(G|C) − u →* ⊥` to `pathwidth ⊥ = 0`, so `pathwidth G[C] ≤ ρ n + 1 ≤ compPotential G C +\\nτ n + ρ n + 1`. -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)\\n    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (hb : IsBasic G) {C : G.ConnectedComponent} {v : V}\\n    (hv : v ∈ compFinset G C) (hpos : 0 < G.degree v) :\\n    (pathwidth (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)) : ℚ) ≤\\n      compPotential G C + τ (Fintype.card V) + ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by\\n  have hρ := h3.nonneg (Fintype.card V)\\n  rcases isBasic_component G hb hv hpos with hcub | ⟨u, _, hred⟩\\n  · -- cubic: (H1) on the component\\n    have hc := h1 _ (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)) (connected_induce_compFinset G C)\\n      (fun w => by rw [degree_induce_compFinset]; exact hcub w (Finset.mem_coe.1 w.2))\\n    simp only [Finset.coe_sort_coe, Fintype.card_coe] at hc\\n    rw [compPotential_cubic G hcub]\\n    have hmono : τ (compFinset G C).card ≤ τ (Fintype.card V) := hτ (Finset.card_le_univ _)\\n    linarith\\n  · -- second kind: one deletion, then (H3) to `⊥`\\n    have h₁ := pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le_restrict G C\\n    have h₂ := pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolate_add_one (restrict G C.supp) u\\n    have h₃ := h3 V _ _ hred\\n    rw [pathwidth_bot] at h₃\\n    have h₄ := compPotential_nonneg G C\\n    have hτn := hτ0 (Fintype.card V)\\n    have h₅ : (pathwidth (G.induce (↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)) : ℚ) ≤\\n        (pathwidth (isolate (restrict G C.supp) u) : ℚ) + 1 := by\\n      exact_mod_cast h₁.trans h₂\\n    push_cast at h₃\\n    linarith\\n\\n/-- **Lemma 5.1 for basic graphs**: `pathwidth B ≤ f⁻(B) + τ n + ρ n + 1` for every reduced basic\\n`B` (the maximum over the components; a connected vertex set with an edge lies in a non-trivial\\ncomponent, and one without edges induces `⊥`). -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_basic_le {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)\\n    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)\\n    (B : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel B.Adj] (hb : IsBasic B) :\\n    (pathwidth B : ℚ) ≤ potentialMinus B + τ (Fintype.card V) + ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by\\n  have hρ := h3.nonneg (Fintype.card V)\\n  have hτn := hτ0 (Fintype.card V)\\n  have hf := potentialMinus_nonneg B\\n  refine pathwidth_le_rat_of_forall_connected B (by linarith) (fun C hc => ?_)\\n  by_cases hdeg : ∀ v ∈ C, B.degree v = 0\\n  · rw [induce_eq_bot_of_forall_degree_eq_zero B hdeg, pathwidth_bot]\\n    push_cast\\n    linarith\\n  · push Not at hdeg\\n    obtain ⟨v, hv, hv0⟩ := hdeg\\n    have hpos : 0 < B.degree v := Nat.pos_of_ne_zero hv0\\n    have hmono := pathwidth_induce_mono B (subset_compFinset_of_connected B hc hv)\\n    have hcomp := pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le h1 h3 hτ hτ0 B hb (self_mem_compFinset B v) hpos\\n    have hle := compPotential_le_potentialMinus B (B.connectedComponentMk v)\\n    have hmono' : (pathwidth (B.induce (↑C : Set V)) : ℚ) ≤\\n        pathwidth (B.induce (↑(compFinset B (B.connectedComponentMk v)) : Set V)) := by\\n      exact_mod_cast hmono\\n    linarith\\n\\n/-- The assembly for any reduction set (Theorem 3.2's conclusion):\\n`pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − X) + |X| ≤ pathwidth B + ρ n + |X| ≤ f⁻(B) + |X| + τ n + 2 ρ n + 1\\n≤ f⁻(G) + τ n + 2 ρ n + 1`. -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_le_of_isReductionSet {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)\\n    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)\\n    {G B : SimpleGraph V} [DecidableRel G.Adj] [DecidableRel B.Adj] {X : Finset V}\\n    (h : IsReductionSet G X B) :\\n    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ potentialMinus G + τ (Fintype.card V) + 2 * ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by\\n  have hX : (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ pathwidth (isolateSet G X) + X.card := by\\n    exact_mod_cast pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card G X\\n  have hred := h3 V _ _ h.reduces\\n  have hbasic := pathwidth_basic_le h1 h3 hτ hτ0 B h.basic\\n  have hcard := h.card_add_le\\n  linarith\\n\\n/-- **A1, Lemma 5.1** (Edwards & McDermid 2015, p. 19, the form its proof establishes): for every\\n`G` with every degree `0` or `≥ 3` and at least one edge,\\n`pathwidth G ≤ f⁻(G) + τ n + 2 ρ n + 1`, conditional on (H1) with a monotone non-negative\\nbudget `τ` and on (H3) with budget `ρ`. -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_le_potentialMinus_of_hypotheses {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)\\n    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (hG : IsSPReduced G) (hne : G ≠ ⊥) :\\n    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ potentialMinus G + τ (Fintype.card V) + 2 * ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by\\n  obtain ⟨X, B, instB, h⟩ := exists_reduction_set G hG hne\\n  exact pathwidth_le_of_isReductionSet h1 h3 hτ hτ0 h\\n\\n/-- **Lemma 5.1 as displayed**: `pathwidth G ≤ Σ_v g(deg v) + τ n + 2 ρ n + 1` for reduced\\n`G ≠ ⊥` (`f⁻ ≤ f`). -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_le_potential_of_hypotheses {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)\\n    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (hG : IsSPReduced G) (hne : G ≠ ⊥) :\\n    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤\\n      ∑ v, g (G.degree v) + τ (Fintype.card V) + 2 * ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by\\n  have h := pathwidth_le_potentialMinus_of_hypotheses h1 h3 hτ hτ0 G hG hne\\n  have h' := potentialMinus_le_potential G\\n  unfold potential at h'\\n  linarith\\n\\n/-! ### Corollary 5.2 -/\\n\\n/-- **A2, Corollary 5.2** (Edwards & McDermid 2015, p. 20): for every `G` and every reduced\\nreduct `B` of `G` (the paper's `r(G)`),\\n`pathwidth G ≤ Σ_v g(deg_B v) + τ n + 3 ρ n + 1`, conditional on (H1) with a monotone\\nnon-negative budget `τ` and on (H3) with budget `ρ`. No `G ≠ ⊥` is needed: when `B = ⊥` the\\nbound is the non-negativity of the budgets. -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_le_degreeSum_of_hypotheses {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)\\n    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) {B : SimpleGraph V} [DecidableRel B.Adj] (hGB : SPReduces G B)\\n    (hB : IsSPReduced B) :\\n    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤\\n      ∑ v, g (B.degree v) + τ (Fintype.card V) + 3 * ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by\\n  have hρ := h3.nonneg (Fintype.card V)\\n  have hτn := hτ0 (Fintype.card V)\\n  have hred := h3 V _ _ hGB\\n  have hpot : potentialMinus B ≤ potential B := potentialMinus_le_potential B\\n  have hp0 : 0 ≤ potential B := potential_nonneg B\\n  have hsum : potential B = ∑ v, g (B.degree v) := rfl\\n  by_cases hne : B = ⊥\\n  · subst hne\\n    rw [pathwidth_bot] at hred\\n    push_cast at hred\\n    linarith\\n  · have hA1 := pathwidth_le_potentialMinus_of_hypotheses h1 h3 hτ hτ0 B hB hne\\n    linarith\\n\\n/-- **Corollary 5.2 with `G`'s own degree histogram**: `pathwidth G ≤ Σ_v g(deg_G v) + τ n +\\n3 ρ n + 1` for every `G`, since reduction never raises a surviving degree and `g` is monotone\\n(R2, `SPReduces.potential_le`). The paper's displayed \\\"`=`\\\" is this \\\"`≤`\\\". -/\\ntheorem pathwidth_le_histogram_of_hypotheses {τ ρ : ℕ → ℚ} (h1 : CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ)\\n    (h3 : ReductionPathwidthBound.{u} ρ) (hτ : Monotone τ) (hτ0 : ∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n)\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\\n    (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤\\n      ∑ v, g (G.degree v) + τ (Fintype.card V) + 3 * ρ (Fintype.card V) + 1 := by\\n  classical\\n  obtain ⟨B, hGB, hB⟩ := exists_reduced_reduct G\\n  have h := pathwidth_le_degreeSum_of_hypotheses h1 h3 hτ hτ0 G hGB hB\\n  have hle : potential B ≤ potential G := SPReduces.potential_le hGB\\n  unfold potential at hle\\n  linarith\\n\\nend MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound\