es (`n = |V|`):","+","+| | statement | budget |","+|---|---|---|","+| **A1** `pathwidth_le_potentialMinus_of_hypotheses` (Lemma 5.1, the form its proof establishes) | every degree `0` or `≥ 3`, `G ≠ ⊥` ⇒ `pw(G) ≤ f⁻(G) + τ(n) + 2ρ(n) + 1` | `τ` once (the cubic component), `ρ` twice (`G − X →* B`; `C − v →* ⊥` inside a second-kind component), `+1` for that `v` |","+| `pathwidth_le_potential_of_hypotheses` (Lemma 5.1 as displayed) | the same with `Σ_v g(deg_G v)` for `f⁻(G)` | the same |","+| **A2** `pathwidth_le_degreeSum_of_hypotheses` (Corollary 5.2) | every `G`, every reduced reduct `B` of `G` ⇒ `pw(G) ≤ Σ_v g(deg_B v) + τ(n) + 3ρ(n) + 1` | one more `ρ` for `G →* B` |","+| `pathwidth_le_histogram_of_hypotheses` (Corollary 5.2, `G`'s own histogram) | every `G` ⇒ `pw(G) ≤ Σ_v g(deg_G v) + τ(n) + 3ρ(n) + 1` | the same; the paper's displayed `=` is this `≤` (plan §0.4 (6)) |","+","+The paper's `τ(n) + O(log n)` is this with `ρ = O(log n)`.","+","+### 9.1 Checked before stated (`09_assembly/check.py`, `check.log`, `summary.json`)","+","+Every graph on 1–8 vertices (`nauty-geng`, 13,598 graphs), pathwidth by the","+subset DP, every deterministic statement of the file in the form Lean proves","+it; 49 s on 8 workers at load 1. The hypotheses (H1), (H3) cannot be checked;","+what the assembly needs from them is *measured* (the last block).","+","+| statement | Lean name | instances to `n = 8` | result |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| PB `pw(⊥) = 0` | `pathwidth_bot` | 13,598 | 0 violations |","+| IX `pw(G) ≤ pw(G − X) + |X|`, **every** `X ⊆ V` | `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card` | 3,305,498 | 0 |","+| IXc `pw(G[Xᶜ]) ≤ pw(G − X)`, every `X` | `pathwidth_induce_compl_le_isolateSet` | 3,305,498 | 0 |","+| I1 `pw(G) ≤ pw(G − v) + 1` | `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolate_add_one` | 107,243 | 0 |","+| CC `G[C₀]` connected, every component `C₀` | `connected_induce_compFinset` | 15,455 | 0 |","+| CR `pw(G[C₀]) ≤ pw(G|C₀)` | `pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le_restrict` | 15,455 | 0 |","+| ID `deg_{G[C₀]} v = deg_G v` | `degree_induce_compFinset` | 107,243 | 0 |","+| CM `C` connected, `v ∈ C` ⇒ `C ⊆ C₀(v)`, `pw(G[C]) ≤ pw(G[C₀])`, **every** connected `C` | `subset_compFinset_of_connected`, `pathwidth_induce_mono` | 2,047,623 | 0 |","+| EZ `C` connected with every degree `0` ⇒ `|C| = 1`, `pw(G[C]) = 0` | `induce_eq_bot_of_forall_degree_eq_zero` | 1,549 | 0 |","+| FC `pw(G) = max_{C connected} pw(G[C])` | `pathwidth_le_rat_of_forall_connected` | 13,598 | 0 |","+| BC reduced basic `B ≠ ⊥`, non-trivial component `C₀`: `compPotential ≤ f⁻`; cubic ⇒ `compPotential = |C₀|/6 − 1/6`; else some `u ∈ C₀` has `r(B|C₀ − u) = ∅` and `pw(B[C₀]) ≤ pw(B|C₀ − u) + 1` | `compPotential_le_potentialMinus`, `pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le` | 622 components (18 cubic, 604 second kind) of 621 graphs | 0 |","+| A1's chain, `X` from Algorithm X: `pw(G) ≤ pw(G − X) + |X|`, `|X| + f⁻(B) ≤ f⁻(G)`, `B` reduced basic non-empty | `pathwidth_le_of_isReductionSet` | 2,964 reduced non-empty graphs | 0 |","+| A2's `f(r(G)) ≤ f(G)` | `SPReduces.potential_le` (item 06) | 13,598 | 0 |","+| the pin: 500 random graphs at `1 ≤ n ≤ 12`, `pw ≤ Σ_{r(G)} g + B(n)` with `B = 3` (`n ≤ 9`, item 02 §2.5, exhaustive), `10/3` (`n = 10`), `4` (`n ≤ 20`) (item 01 §1.3, the record) | — (the budgets are abstract) | 500 | 500 hold; largest deficit 3 at `n = 11` (`pw 3`, main term 0) |","+","+**Kill checks: none fired; zero violations.** The same 500 random graphs also","+passed every deterministic check above (6,660 `(G, X)` pairs, 8,425 connected","+sets, 22 basic components).","+","+**What the budgets must reach at these sizes** (maxima to `n = 8`, exact","+rationals; the paper's unspecified `o(n)` and `O(log n)`, measured):","+`pw − f⁻` over reduced non-empty graphs **17/6** (item 02's value to 9);","+`pw(G) − f(r(G))` **3**, `pw(G) − f(G)` **8/3**; the cubic base case","+`pw(C₀) − (|C₀|/6 − 1/6)` over cubic components **17/6** (`n = 8`; `5/2` at","+`K₄`); the (H3) gap at `⊥` for second-kind components, `pw(B|C₀ − u)` with `u`","+chosen best, **3** (`n = 7–8`; so `ρ(8) ≥ 3` is what a second-kind component","+on 8 vertices needs); the (H3) gap `pw(G − X) − pw(B)` along A1's chain **1**;","+the (H3) gap `pw(G) − pw(r(G))` along A2's **3** (item 02's measurement).","+Measured on every graph to 8 vertices and nothing else; these are not","+constants of anything.","+","+### 9.2 The two named hypotheses, verbatim","+","+```lean","+/-- (H1) The cubic base case, a named `Prop` with budget `τ`. -/","+def CubicPathwidthBound (τ : ℕ → ℚ) : Prop :=","+  ∀ (W : Type u) [Fintype W] [DecidableEq W] (G : SimpleGraph W) [DecidableRel G.Adj],","+    G.Connected → (∀ v, G.degree v = 3) →","+      (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ (Fintype.card W : ℚ) / 6 - 1 / 6 + τ (Fintype.card W)","+","+/-- (H3) The reduction lemma, a named `Prop` with budget `ρ`. -/","+def ReductionPathwidthBound (ρ : ℕ → ℚ) : Prop :=","+  ∀ (W : Type u) [Fintype W] [DecidableEq W] (G H : SimpleGraph W),","+    SPReduces G H → (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ pathwidth H + ρ (Fintype.card W)","+```","+","+Their docstrings quote the sources (plan §0.2): for (H1), Edwards & McDermid","+p. 19 — \"Fomin and Høie [12] showed that a 3-regular graph `G` with `m` edges","+has pathwidth at most `(1/9 + o(1)) m + O(log n) = (1/6 + o(1)) n + O(log n)`.","+Hence for 3-regular graphs, there is a function `τ`, with `τ(n) = o(n)`, such","+that `pw(G) ≤ n/6 − 1/6 + τ(n) + O(log n)` (the negative term is needed","+below). We can also assume that `τ` is an increasing function of `n`\" — and","+Fomin & Høie's Theorem 5 — \"For any `ε > 0`, there exists an integer `n_ε`","+such that for every graph `G` with maximum vertex degree at most three and","+with `|V(G)| > n_ε`, `pw(G) ≤ (1/6 + ε)|V(G)|`\"; for (H3), p. 20 — \"It follows","+from the results of [21] that `pw(G) ≤ |X_G| + pw(G − X_G)` and that","+`pw(G − X_G) = pw(r(G − X_G)) + O(log n)`\" — and p. 5 — \"series-parallel","+graphs have treewidth at most 2. The pathwidth of these graphs is","+`O(log n)`\" (the case `H = ⊥`), with the note that [21] is not held","+(`literature/MISSING.md`). Neither is asserted anywhere: no `theorem`,","+`instance` or `axiom` has either as its conclusion","+(`test_pathwidth_assembly_proved_names_are_theorems_in_the_lean_file` checks","+this mechanically), exactly as `EdgeSearchMonotonicity` in","+`Complex/EdgeSearch.lean`. The `Prop`s are universe-polymorphic (`Type u`),","+so that a theorem about a graph on `V : Type u` can apply them to the induced","+subgraph on a component, whose vertex type lives in the same universe.","+","+**Side conditions on the budgets, beyond (H1) and (H3).** The final theorems","+take `Monotone τ` (the paper's \"we can also assume that `τ` is an increasing","+function\"; needed because (H1) is applied to a component on `|C| ≤ n`","+vertices) and `∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n` (needed because a graph may have no cubic","+component at all, and then the `τ` term is pure slack that must not be","+negative; the paper's `o(n)` is a non-negative error term, so this is a","+reading, not a strengthening). `∀ n, 0 ≤ ρ n` is **derived** from (H3)","+(`ReductionPathwidthBound.nonneg`: `G →* G` in zero steps on `ULift (Fin n)`),","+and `Monotone ρ` is not needed, because every use of (H3) is on the ambient","+vertex type `V` (removed vertices are isolated, plan §0.5) — the design's","+one-vertex-type convention pays here.","+","+### 9.3 The statements and their proofs (namespace `MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound`; 21 theorems, 2 definitions)","+","+| name | statement | proof |","+|---|---|---|","+| `ReductionPathwidthBound.nonneg` | `ReductionPathwidthBound ρ → ∀ n, 0 ≤ ρ n` | (H3) at `G = H = ⊥` on `ULift.{u} (Fin n)`, `SPReduces.refl`, `Fintype.card_ulift`, `card_fin` |","+| `pathwidth_bot` | `pathwidth (⊥ : SimpleGraph V) = 0` | the decomposition with bags `{v : e v = i}` for `e = Fintype.equivFin V`, `i ≤ |V|`; `width_le_of_forall_card_le` with `card_le_one` from `e.injective` |","+| `pathwidth_induce_compl_le_isolateSet` | `pathwidth G[Xᶜ] ≤ pathwidth (G − X)` | `pathwidth_le_of_injective` with the hom `Subtype.val : G[Xᶜ] →g G − X` |","+| `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card` | `pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − X) + |X|` | `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl G Xᶜ` (`TreeBound`), `compl_compl`, the previous |","+| `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolate_add_one` | `pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (G − w) + 1` | `X = {w}`, `isolateSet_singleton` |","+| `pathwidth_le_rat_of_forall_connected` | `0 ≤ b → (∀ C, G[C].Connected → (pathwidth G[C] : ℚ) ≤ b) → (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ b` | `pathwidth_induce_univ` (`CutLemma`), `pathwidth_induce_le_of_forall_connected` (`TreeBound`) at `k = ⌊b⌋₊`, `Nat.le_floor`, `Nat.floor_le` |","+| `coe_compFinset` | `↑(compFinset G C) = C.supp` | `mem_compFinset_iff_mem_supp` |","+| `connected_induce_compFinset` | `G[compFinset G C].Connected` | Mathlib's `ConnectedComponent.maximal_connected_induce_supp` |","+| `degree_induce_of_forall_adj_mem` | `[Fintype s]`, `(∀ u, G.Adj v u → u ∈ s) → (G.induce s).degree v = G.degree v` | `Finset.card_bij` with `a ↦ ↑a` on the neighbour finsets |","+| `degree_induce_compFinset` | `v ∈ C₀ ⇒ deg_{G[C₀]} v = deg_G v` | the previous with `insert_neighborFinset_subset_compFinset` (item 08) |","+| `subset_compFinset_of_connected` | `G[C].Connected → v ∈ C → C ⊆ compFinset G (mk v)` | `Connected.preconnected`, `Reachable.map` along `Embedding.induce`, `mem_compFinset_mk` |","+| `pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le_restrict` | `pathwidth G[C₀] ≤ pathwidth (G|C₀.supp)` | `pathwidth_le_of_injective` with `Subtype.val` |","+| `induce_eq_bot_of_forall_degree_eq_zero` | `(∀ v ∈ C, G.degree v = 0) → G[C] = ⊥` | `ext`; `degree_pos_iff_exists_adj` |","+| `compPotential_le_potentialMinus` | `compPotential G C ≤ f⁻(G)` | `potentialMinus_eq_sum_compPotential`, `single_le_sum`, `compPotential_nonneg` (item 05) |","+| `pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le` | (H1), (H3), `Monotone τ`, `0 ≤ τ`; `IsBasic G`; `v ∈ C₀`, `0 < deg v` ⇒ `(pathwidth G[C₀] : ℚ) ≤ compPotential G C₀ + τ n + ρ n + 1` | `isBasic_component` (item 08); **cubic**: (H1) on `G[C₀]` with `connected_induce_compFinset` and `degree_induce_compFinset`, `Finset.coe_sort_coe`/`Fintype.card_coe`, `compPotential_cubic` (item 08), `hτ (card_le_univ)`, `ρ ≥ 0`; **second kind**: `pathwidth_induce_compFinset_le_restrict`, `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolate_add_one`, (H3) on `(G|C₀) − u →* ⊥`, `pathwidth_bot`, `compPotential_nonneg`, `τ ≥ 0` |","+| `pathwidth_basic_le` | (H1), (H3), `Monotone τ`, `0 ≤ τ`; `IsBasic B` ⇒ `(pathwidth B : ℚ) ≤ f⁻(B) + τ n + ρ n + 1` | `pathwidth_le_rat_of_forall_connected` (`0 ≤ b` from `f⁻ ≥ 0`, `τ ≥ 0`, `ρ ≥ 0`); for a connected `C`: if every degree on `C` is `0`, `induce_eq_bot_of_forall_degree_eq_zero` and `pathwidth_bot`; else `subset_compFinset_of_connected`, `pathwidth_induce_mono` (`CutLemma`), the previous, `compPotential_le_potentialMinus` |","+| `pathwidth_le_of_isReductionSet` | (H1), (H3), `Monotone τ`, `0 ≤ τ`; `IsReductionSet G X B` ⇒ `(pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ f⁻(G) + τ n + 2ρ n + 1` | `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card`, (H3) on `h.reduces`, `pathwidth_basic_le` on `B`, `h.card_add_le`, `linarith` |","+| **A1** `pathwidth_le_potentialMinus_of_hypotheses` | … `IsSPReduced G → G ≠ ⊥ → (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ f⁻(G) + τ n + 2ρ n + 1` | `exists_reduction_set` (T1, item 08) and the previous |","+| `pathwidth_le_potential_of_hypotheses` | … `→ (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ Σ_v g (G.degree v) + τ n + 2ρ n + 1` | A1, `potentialMinus_le_potential` |","+| **A2** `pathwidth_le_degreeSum_of_hypotheses` | … `SPReduces G B → IsSPReduced B → (pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ Σ_v g (B.degree v) + τ n + 3ρ n + 1` | (H3) on `G →* B`; `B = ⊥`: `pathwidth_bot` and the non-negativity of `f`, `τ`, `ρ`; `B ≠ ⊥`: A1 on `B`, `potentialMinus_le_potential` |","+| `pathwidth_le_histogram_of_hypotheses` | … `(pathwidth G : ℚ) ≤ Σ_v g (G.degree v) + τ n + 3ρ n + 1` for every `G` | `exists_reduced_reduct` (item 06) under `classical`, A2, `SPReduces.potential_le` (R2 with W2, item 06) |","+","+### 9.4 What is proved, what is cited","+","+| | status | where |","+|---|---|---|","+| the weights `g`, `g'` and Lemmas 8.1, 8.3–8.5, property 6 | **proved** | `Weights.lean` (item 03) |","+| the cut lemma and its iterated form (independent of everything else) | **proved** | `CutLemma.lean` (item 04) |","+| the potential `f`, `f⁻` per component, one-deletion accounting (equations (2)–(5)) | **proved** | `Potential.lean` (item 05) |","+| the reduction system, termination, degree monotonicity, deletion–reduction commutation (replaces Lemma 3.1's appeal to [21]'s confluence) | **proved** | `SPReduction.lean` (item 06) |","+| the step inequality `1 + f⁻(G*) ≤ f⁻(G)` in all four cases (pp. 11–12) | **proved** | `Step.lean` (item 07) |","+| Theorem 3.2, the reduction theorem | **proved**, unconditional | `ReductionTheorem.lean` (item 08) |","+| `pw(G) ≤ |X| + pw(G − X)` (the paper attributes it to [21]) | **proved** | `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card` |","+| `pw(G) = max_i pw(G_i)` | **proved** (the `≤` direction, which is the one used) | `pathwidth_le_rat_of_forall_connected` |","+| (H1) the cubic base case, Fomin & Høie 2006 Theorem 5 | **cited**, named `Prop` `CubicPathwidthBound τ`; budget measured on the record (item 01 §1.4: `3.833` to 16 vertices exhaustively, `4.5` on the 42 certified cubic graphs to 120) | hypothesis of A1, A2 |","+| (H3) the reduction lemma, Kneis et al. 2009 | **cited**, named `Prop` `ReductionPathwidthBound ρ`; shape measured (item 02 §2.5: `pw(G) − pw(r(G)) ≤ 3` to 9 vertices) | hypothesis of A1, A2 |","+| `Monotone τ`, `0 ≤ τ n` | **assumed** (side conditions on the budget, §9.2) | hypotheses of A1, A2 |","+| `0 ≤ ρ n` | **derived** from (H3) | `ReductionPathwidthBound.nonneg` |","+| Lemma 5.1, Corollary 5.2 | **proved conditional on the two `Prop`s and the two side conditions** | this file |","+| Theorem 5.3 (the Edwards–Farr averaging lemma) | **not formalised**; verified numerically in item 01 §1.6 | — |","+","+The final theorems have **exactly four hypotheses beyond the graph's own**:","+`CubicPathwidthBound τ`, `ReductionPathwidthBound ρ`, `Monotone τ`,","+`∀ n, 0 ≤ τ n`. No upstream item left a gap, so nothing else is carried.","+","+### 9.5 Choices beyond §2.6 and the item's wording","+","+1. **The `Prop`s are universe-polymorphic** (`∀ (W : Type u)`), not over `Type`","+   as the item wrote: the theorems are stated for `V : Type u` like every","+   file of the development, and (H1) is applied to the induced subgraph on a","+   component, whose vertex type `↥(↑(compFinset G C) : Set V)` lives in `Type u`.","+   Statements write `CubicPathwidthBound.{u} τ` so that the level is fixed.","+2. **The side condition `0 ≤ τ n`** is not in the item or in §2.6, which had","+   `Monotone τ → Monotone ρ →`. It is needed (a second-kind component's bound","+   `ρ n + 1 ≤ compPotential + τ n + ρ n + 1` has `τ n` as slack), and `Monotone ρ`","+   is not (every use of (H3) is on `V`); `0 ≤ ρ n` is derived. §9.2.","+3. **The maximum over components is `pathwidth_le_rat_of_forall_connected`**,","+   stated for every connected vertex set and in `ℚ` (through `⌊b⌋₊`), not the","+   §2.6 pair `pathwidth_eq_pathwidth_induce_supp` / `pathwidth_le_max_components`","+   over `restrict`: `pathwidth_induce_le_of_forall_connected` already quantifies","+   over connected finsets, and a connected finset with an edge is pulled into","+   its component by `subset_compFinset_of_connected` and `pathwidth_induce_mono`.","+   `pathwidth_eq_pathwidth_induce_supp` is therefore not stated (not needed).","+4. **`CutLemma.lean` is used, not merely imported**: `pathwidth_induce_univ`","+   and `pathwidth_induce_mono` come from it, so the item's \"not needed by the","+   proof\" is corrected — its bisection theorems are what the assembly does not","+   use.","+5. **`pathwidth_basic_le` needs no `B ≠ ⊥`** and **A2 needs no `G ≠ ⊥`**","+   (both in the item's wording): for `B = ⊥` the bounds are the","+   non-negativity of `f`, `f⁻`, `τ`, `ρ`. A1 keeps `G ≠ ⊥` because T1 has it.","+6. **`degree_induce_of_forall_adj_mem` is proved by a bijection**, not from","+   Mathlib's `degree_induce_of_neighborSet_subset`: that lemma's `Fintype`","+   instance on the induced neighbour set is built from a `DecidablePred`, and","+   unifying it with the instance of a coerced finset made the elaborator","+   unfold `compFinset` (a classical filter) until the heartbeat limit. The","+   bijection keeps the goal's own instances; the general form takes","+   `[Fintype ↥s]` explicitly.","+7. **`pathwidth_le_of_isReductionSet`** is the assembly for any reduction set,","+   and A1 is its application to T1's — so the arithmetic of Lemma 5.1's last","+   display is one `linarith` over four facts.","+8. **`pathwidth_bot` on any `V`** (the development had it for `Fin 4` only,","+   `Sandwich.lean`): bags indexed by `Fintype.equivFin`.","+","+### 9.6 Axiom lines, the sandwich stage, tests, regenerate","+","+- 21 new `#print axioms` lines in `paper1/axiom_check.lean`","+  (`09_assembly/axiom_check.log`); `make -C paper1/latex axioms`: **577","+  theorems checked, 0 failures**, every line `[propext, Classical.choice,","+  Quot.sound]` — the hypotheses are arguments, not axioms, so the final","+  theorems rest on the standard three like everything else. `lake build`","+  passes (`09_assembly/lake_build.log`); the file builds in 1.3 s.","+- `PATHWIDTH_ASSEMBLY_PROVED` (21 names) is folded into","+  `learning.sandwich.ALL_PROVED` (371 names in all); `python -m learning.sandwich","+  --stage lean` audits them (`09_assembly/sandwich_lean.log`, every row","+  `proved / True / propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound / False`).","+- `python -m learning.sandwich --stage degree_bound` has three new rows on the","+  stage's 500 random graphs at 1–12 vertices (`09_assembly/sandwich.log`; **22","+  rows, 5,793 checks, 0 violations**): the item's numerical pin","+  `pw ≤ Σ_{r(G)} g + B(n)` with item 02's `B(n)` (500 of 500), the deletion","+  lemma with one random `X` per graph, and `pw(G) = max_C pw(G[C])`.","+  `reports/sandwich_tables.md` is regenerated by it and now carries the 22 rows.","+- Tests: 3 new in `tests/test_edwards_mcdermid.py` (50 in all): the","+  deterministic statements in the Lean form on 200 random graphs at 1–11","+  vertices with isolated vertices; the brute-force summary's counts and zero","+  violations; the 21 names declared (namespaces resolved) / imported /","+  audited, no `sorry`, no `axiom`, no `instance`, the two `Prop`s present as","+  `def … : Prop` and **never concluded by any theorem**, the seven theorems","+  that take the four hypotheses, and the `2 ρ` / `3 ρ` budgets in the text.","+- Regenerate: `nice -n 19 python3 reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/09_assembly/check.py --max-n 8 --workers 8`","+  (49 s); `cd lean && lake build`; `make -C paper1/latex axioms`;","+  `python -m learning.sandwich --stage lean`; `python -m learning.sandwich --stage degree_bound`;","+  `python -m pytest tests/test_edwards_mcdermid.py -q`.","+","+### 9.7 The Appendix A rows, drafted for item 10 (not yet in the paper)","+","+For `paper1/latex/sec9a_appendix_lean.tex`, in the format of its existing rows","+(`\\leanentry{label}{text} \\leannames{names} \\\\`); item 10 places them and","+edits the two sentences around `\\citet{EdwardsMcDermid2015}` in","+`sec9e_appendix_random.tex`:","+","+```latex","+\\leanentry{reduction-theorem}{Theorem~3.2 of \\citet{EdwardsMcDermid2015}, the reduction theorem","+  (Appendix~\\ref{app:random}): every graph with every degree $0$ or $\\ge 3$ has a vertex set $X$","+  with $G - X$ reducing to a non-empty basic graph $B$ and $|X| + f^-(B) \\le f^-(G)$; unconditional,","+  with the step inequality in all four cases and a local commutation lemma in place of the","+  confluence appeal} \\leannames{exists_reduction_set, one_add_potentialMinus_le, SPReduces.isolateSet_comm, potential_isolate} \\\\","+\\leanentry{degree-bound}{Lemma~5.1 and Corollary~5.2 of \\citet{EdwardsMcDermid2015}","+  (Appendix~\\ref{app:random}): $\\mathrm{pw}(G) \\le \\sum_v g(d_G(v)) + \\tau(n) + 3\\rho(n) + 1$ for","+  every $G$, conditional on the two cited results stated as named propositions and never","+  asserted --- the cubic base case \\path{CubicPathwidthBound} with budget $\\tau$","+  \\citep[Theorem~5]{FominHoie2006} and the reduction lemma \\path{ReductionPathwidthBound} with","+  budget $\\rho$ (Kneis et al.\\ 2009) --- and on $\\tau$ monotone and non-negative; the paper gives","+  no constants} \\leannames{pathwidth_le_histogram_of_hypotheses, pathwidth_le_degreeSum_of_hypotheses, pathwidth_le_potentialMinus_of_hypotheses, pathwidth_basic_le, CubicPathwidthBound, ReductionPathwidthBound} \\\\","+```","+","+(`FominHoie2006` is a bibliography key to be checked by item 10's `make","+refs`; if absent, the citation is written out.)","+","+### 9.8 Kill verdict, and what this does not claim","+","+**Kill verdict: none** (the item has no kill criterion). No upstream item left","+a gap; the final theorems carry no hypothesis beyond (H1), (H3) and the two","+side conditions on `τ` of §9.2.","+","+**Does not claim.** (H1) or (H3) — cited, named, never asserted, and not","+provable here (plan §0.3: (H3) would need the series-parallel pathwidth bound","+and Mathlib has no series-parallel graphs); any value of `τ` or `ρ` (the","+maxima of §9.1 are measurements on every graph to 8 vertices and on the","+record, not constants); Theorem 5.3 (the averaging lemma is Edwards & Farr's;","+item 01 §1.6 verified it numerically); that the budgets `τ + 2ρ + 1` and","+`τ + 3ρ + 1` are tight — the `+1` is the deleted vertex of a second-kind","+component (the paper absorbs it into `O(log n)`), and the count of `ρ`s","+follows the proof's uses of (H3), not a lower bound; that the `≤` of","+`pathwidth_le_histogram_of_hypotheses` is ever strict beyond what R2 gives;","+that `pathwidth_bot` or the deletion lemma are new (they are folklore;","+Mathlib lacks them in this form, and \"we found no prior statement\" is not","+claimed either); that Fomin & Høie's Theorem 5 is formalised (item 04 §4.3","+states its one-level transfer and does not prove it)."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/edwards_mcdermid.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JzkrueLVY2St5rQtSCNKrZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
